EXAM_DATA.papers["2010-english-one"] = {"id":"2010-english-one","year":2010,"label":"2010 英语一","era":"modern","sourceUrl":"https://english-exam.lazynote.cn/kaoyan/paper/2010-english-one/","timeLimitMin":180,"scoreMode":"estimated","parts":[{"id":"section1","kind":"cloze","title":"Section I 完形填空","directions":"Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET . (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section1-1","text":"In 1924 America's National Research Council sent two engineers to supervise a series of experiments at a telephone-parts factory called the Hawthorne Plant near Chicago. It hoped they would learn how shop-floor lighting   {{1}}   workers' productivity. Instead, the studies ended   {{2}}   giving their name to the \"Hawthorne effect,\" the extremely influential idea that the very   {{3}}   of being experimented upon changed subjects' behavior."},{"id":"p-section1-2","text":"The idea arose because of the   {{4}}   behavior of the women in the plant. According to   {{5}}   of the experiments, their hourly output rose when lighting was increased, but also when it was dimmed. It did not   {{6}}   what was done in the experiment;   {{7}}   something was changed, productivity rose. A(n)   {{8}}   that they were being experimented upon seemed to be   {{9}}   to alter workers' behavior   {{10}}   itself."},{"id":"p-section1-3","text":"After several decades, the same data were   {{11}}   to econometric analysis. The Hawthorne experiments had another surprise in store.   {{12}}   the descriptions on record, no systematic   {{13}}   was found that levels of productivity were related to changes in lighting."},{"id":"p-section1-4","text":"It turns out that the peculiar way of conducting the experiments may have led to   {{14}}   interpretations of what happened.   {{15}}   , lighting was always changed on a Sunday. When work started again on Monday, output   {{16}}   rose compared with the previous Saturday and   {{17}}   to rise for the next couple of days.   {{18}}   , a comparison with data for weeks when there was no experimentation showed that output always went up on Mondays. Workers   {{19}}   to be diligent for the first few days of the week in any case, before   {{20}}   a plateau and then slackening off. This suggests that the alleged \"Hawthorne effect\" is hard to pin down."}]},"questions":[{"n":1,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"affected"},{"key":"B","text":"achieved"},{"key":"C","text":"extracted"},{"key":"D","text":"restored"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"1.","reason":"研究目的是考察照明对产量的影响 本句的关键线索是 It hoped they would learn how shop-floor lighting __(1)__ workers' productivity——委员会派人去研究「照明怎样作用于产量」，因此空格动词应表达「对……产生作用/影响」这一中性关系，而非「实现、提取、恢复」等带特定方向的语义。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"affected 意为「影响、作用于」，正好对应「研究照明如何影响产量」这一开放性目的，不预设结果方向，与 learn how shop-floor lighting __(1)__ workers' productivity 严丝合缝。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"achieved 意为「取得、达成」，宾语通常是 goal、success 一类成果名词。说「照明取得了产量」明显荒谬，且研究本意只是观察作用关系，并非证明照明能创造产量。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"extracted 表「提取、抽取」，需要一个可被抽出的实体作宾语，主语也应是有意识的主体；此处主语是无生命的 lighting，宾语是抽象的 productivity，搭配上完全不成立。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"restored 表「使恢复」，预设产量先前曾下降；但原文只说研究照明与产量的关系，并未交代产量曾下降，前提不成立，被排除。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":2,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"at"},{"key":"B","text":"up"},{"key":"C","text":"with"},{"key":"D","text":"off"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"2.","reason":"end up doing 表「最终落得做……」 本句 the studies ended __(2)__ giving their name to the \"Hawthorne effect\" 想表达「这些研究最终以「为霍桑效应命名」收场」，对应英语固定短语 end up doing sth.（最终、结果做某事），所以空格应填 up。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"at 与 end 不构成固定短语来表达「最终做某事」，且 at 后通常接地点或时间点，与后接动名词的句式不匹配。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"up 与 end 构成 end up doing sth. 这一高频短语，表「最终落得做……、结果做……」，正好契合「研究本想测光照影响、结果反倒为霍桑效应命名」的意外反转语气。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"with 与 end 搭配时，强调「以某物作结尾」，宾语通常是具体的结尾节目/段落（end with a song），且不强调「意外结果」这层含义，与本句动名词主动作的语气不吻合。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"off 与 end 几乎不构成固定短语；个别用法如 end off with 也是「以……收尾」，且必带 with，不能直接接 doing。语义、形式两不合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":3,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"truth"},{"key":"B","text":"sight"},{"key":"C","text":"act"},{"key":"D","text":"proof"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"3.","reason":"强调「被实验」这件事本身就改变了行为 线索在 the very __(3)__ of being experimented upon changed subjects' behavior——霍桑效应的核心定义是：被观察/被实验「这一行为本身」就会改变受试者表现。所以名词必须能表「行为、举动」，即 act of doing sth.。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"truth 意为「真相、真理」，the very truth of ... 强调「关于……的真相」，会把焦点引向「实验真相」，但句子主语是「真相改变行为」，逻辑不通。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"sight 是「看见、景象」，多接具体可视对象（the sight of blood），用于抽象 of being experimented upon 既不地道，也无法表达「行为本身致使改变」这层定义。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"act 表「行为、举动」，the very act of being experimented upon 即「正是被实验这一行为本身」，精准对应霍桑效应「不必更改什么，被观察这件事自身就足以改变行为」的核心含义。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"proof 表「证据、证明」，the very proof of ... 是「关于……的确凿证据」，会让句意变成「证据改变了行为」，与作者强调「被实验本身就足以改变行为」的因果链相反。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":4,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"controversial"},{"key":"B","text":"perplexing"},{"key":"C","text":"mischievous"},{"key":"D","text":"ambiguous"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"4.","reason":"光强、光弱产量都上升，让人摸不着头脑 下一句 their hourly output rose when lighting was increased, but also when it was dimmed 给出原因——不论光线增强还是减弱，产量都上升，这种「按理不该同时发生」的反常恰好让研究者百思不得其解，对应「令人困惑」一义。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"controversial 强调「引发争论、各方意见对立」，但文中并未提到研究者们就该行为产生了不同意见，只是「不论调亮调暗产量都升」让人费解，与「争议」不在一个维度。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"perplexing 意为「使人困惑的」，正对应 their hourly output rose when lighting was increased, but also when it was dimmed 这种「调高调低都升」的反直觉现象，研究者无法用常识解释，因而催生了新假说。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"mischievous 表「恶作剧的、爱搞怪的」，多用于孩童行为；工人生产数据呈现的反常与「调皮」毫无关系，色彩、对象都错。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"ambiguous 强调「语义不清、可作多种解释」，多用于陈述、措辞；这里描述的是行为带来的反直觉结果，并不是行为「意义模棱两可」，方向偏离。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":5,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"requirements"},{"key":"B","text":"explanations"},{"key":"C","text":"accounts"},{"key":"D","text":"assessments"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"5.","reason":"下文是实验结果的描述 线索是接下来的内容 their hourly output rose when lighting was increased, but also when it was dimmed——这是对实验观察结果的「描述/记述」。能与之搭配的是「实验记述/记录」，即 accounts of the experiments。P3 中 __(12)__ the descriptions on record 也回应了这种「记录式描述」的存在。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"requirements 指「要求、规定」，但下文说的是产量怎样变化的事实，不是实验提出的要求；「依据实验的要求，产量上升了」逻辑不通。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"explanations 意为「解释」。下一句仅陈述现象 output rose，并未给出原因分析，与「解释」的语义不符；且 P3 后文用 descriptions on record 回指此处，提示更应是「记述」。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"accounts 在此表「记述、描述、报告」，正好与下文 their hourly output rose when lighting was increased, but also when it was dimmed 这种事实陈述相吻合；并和后文 __(12)__ the descriptions on record 形成同义回指，互为线索。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"assessments 意为「评估、评价」，强调价值判断；下文是数据变化的客观陈述，没有评估或评价之意，方向偏离。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":6,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"conclude"},{"key":"B","text":"matter"},{"key":"C","text":"indicate"},{"key":"D","text":"work"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"6.","reason":"无论做了什么，产量都上升 线索在本句与紧随其后的分句 It did not __(6)__ what was done in the experiment; __(7)__ something was changed, productivity rose——分号后说「只要变了什么，产量就上升」，反推前半句要表达「实验里做了什么并不重要」，所以空格动词需是 matter。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"conclude 表「下结论」，「它没有就实验做什么得出结论」与下文「只要变了什么产量就升」的「无关紧要」之意完全脱节。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"matter 作动词意为「要紧、重要」，It did not matter what was done「做了什么并不重要」是高频固定句型；与分号后 __(7)__ something was changed, productivity rose 形成「不在于做了什么、只在于变了什么」的精准呼应。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"indicate 表「表明、暗示」，主语通常为「数据、事实」，且否定式 did not indicate what was done 变成「没有表明做了什么」，与作者要说「这无关紧要」的主旨南辕北辙。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"work 作「起作用、奏效」时主语应是某方法或某事物；It did not work what was done 不合语法、也偏离句意，属于硬塞动词。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":7,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"as far as"},{"key":"B","text":"for fear that"},{"key":"C","text":"in case that"},{"key":"D","text":"so long as"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"7.","reason":"「只要……就」的充分条件关系 前句 It did not __(6)__ what was done in the experiment 否定「做了什么」的作用，分号后想说「只要变了什么，产量就上升」——这是充分条件，对应 so long as「只要」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"as far as 表「就……而言、在……范围内」，常用 as far as I know，强调范围限度；此处需要的是「只要……就」的条件关系，方向不对。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"for fear that 表「唯恐、以免」，前后是主观避免某结果的目的关系，但本句是客观陈述「变化即上升」的对应关系，没有人想避免任何事，逻辑错。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"in case that 表「以防、万一」，带假设和预防意味，且 in case 后一般不接 that；本句陈述的是反复观察到的客观规律，不是预防性假设。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"so long as 意为「只要」，表充分条件；与前句「做什么不重要」形成「不重要的是做什么、重要的是变化本身」的递进，再加分号后 productivity rose 构成「只要变就升」的对应，是唯一逻辑通畅项。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":8,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"awareness"},{"key":"B","text":"expectation"},{"key":"C","text":"sentiment"},{"key":"D","text":"illusion"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"8.","reason":"「察觉自己在被实验」是事实，不是错觉或期待 线索是同位语从句 that they were being experimented upon——工人确实在被实验，这是客观事实；他们对此的心理是「意识到、知道」，所以名词应表「知晓、意识」，即 awareness。这一含义也回指概念定义中的 the very __(3)__ of being experimented upon changed subjects' behavior。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"awareness 意为「意识、察觉」，an awareness that ... 表「意识到……这一事实」，与从句内容「正在被实验」相符，并精准对接霍桑效应的核心：被试者「意识到自己被观察」就足以改变行为。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"expectation 表「期望、预期」，所接的从句通常是「将要发生的事」（that something will happen）；这里从句是 they were being experimented upon「正被实验」，时态是正在进行，不是期待中的未来事件。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"sentiment 表「情绪、看法」，常接介词短语而少接 that-从句作同位语，更不与「正在被实验」这类事实陈述匹配；且情绪本身不构成霍桑效应的解释机制。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"illusion 表「错觉、幻觉」，强调与事实不符；但工人确实在被实验，并非错觉，用 illusion 会让句子变成「他们错以为自己被实验」，与原文逻辑相反。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":9,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"suitable"},{"key":"B","text":"excessive"},{"key":"C","text":"enough"},{"key":"D","text":"abundant"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"9.","reason":"「单凭这一意识就足以改变行为」的程度副意 线索是结尾的 to alter workers' behavior __(10)__ itself——「单凭它自己就改变工人行为」。前面 seemed to be ___ to alter 表「似乎足以改变」，意思是「程度足够」，对应 enough（be enough to do = 足以做……）。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"suitable 表「合适、适宜的」，强调与某需求相称，不传达「程度足够引发结果」之意，且 suitable to do 远不如 enough to do 常用。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"excessive 表「过度、过量的」，带贬义；作者只是客观说「这种意识足以改变行为」，没有「过度」的色彩。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"enough 用作形容词或副词时常构成 be enough to do sth.「足以做某事」；此处「这种意识似乎就足以改变工人行为」正是该结构的典型语义，与下个空 by itself「单凭自身」形成「程度足够+独立作用」的完整表达。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"abundant 表「丰富、大量的」，多修饰资源、证据等可计量事物（abundant resources/evidence），与单数抽象名词 awareness 搭配生硬，且不传达「足以」的关键含义。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":10,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"about"},{"key":"B","text":"for"},{"key":"C","text":"on"},{"key":"D","text":"by"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"10.","reason":"强调「单凭这种意识自身」改变行为 线索是前面的 A(n) __(8)__ that they were being experimented upon seemed to be __(9)__ to alter workers' behavior __(10)__ itself——主语「这种意识」充当唯一原因，意思是「单凭它自身就改变行为」，对应 by itself「独自、单凭它自己」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"about 与 itself 不存在「单凭自身」的搭配义；about itself 通常表「关于它自己」，语义错配。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"for 与 itself 搭出 for itself「为它自己」，强调对象/受益方；这里要的是「独自起作用」的方式，意思不对。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"on 与 itself 几乎不构成习惯短语来表「独自」；on one's own 才是「独自」的常见说法，与本题不同。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"by 与 itself 构成 by itself「单凭它自己、独自地」，正好补足 enough to alter ... by itself「足以单凭自身改变……」的完整表达，与霍桑效应「不必额外干预、被观察即可致变」的内涵相印证。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"compared"},{"key":"B","text":"shown"},{"key":"C","text":"subjected"},{"key":"D","text":"conveyed"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"11.","reason":"把旧数据「拿来做」计量经济分析 线索是 After several decades, the same data were __(11)__ to econometric analysis——「几十年后，同一批数据被___给计量分析」。语义是「拿来做某种分析、施以某种检验」，对应 be subjected to「被施以、接受」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"compared 与 to 搭出 be compared to「与……相比」，需要的是同类比较对象；但 econometric analysis 是一种「方法」，不能作为被比较的对象，搭配方向错。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"shown 接 to + sb. 表「展示给某人」；与「计量经济分析」这种方法搭配不通，且 show to analysis 不构成熟词组。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"subjected 与 to 构成 be subjected to「遭受、被施以」，be subjected to analysis 即「接受/被施以分析」，是科研文体里的标配；与「几十年后回头用新方法重新分析旧数据」语境精准对应。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"conveyed 与 to 搭配表「把……传达给某人」，对象通常是人或机构；用于 analysis 不合搭配，意思也错。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Contrary to"},{"key":"B","text":"Consistent with"},{"key":"C","text":"Parallel with"},{"key":"D","text":"Peculiar to"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"12.","reason":"旧记述说有关系、新分析说没关系 前文 P2 According to __(5)__ of the experiments, their hourly output rose when lighting was increased, but also when it was dimmed 显示旧记述说产量随光照变化；本句 no systematic __(13)__ was found that levels of productivity were related to changes in lighting 说新分析未发现产量与光照相关的系统性证据——结论相反，对应 Contrary to「与……相反」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"Contrary to 表「与……相反」，直接呼应前文旧记述「产量随光照变化」与本句「找不到产量与光照相关的证据」之间的反差，是 P3 最关键的转折信号。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"Consistent with 表「与……一致」，若代入则等于说「新分析与旧记述一致地未发现相关性」，但旧记述明明声称发现了相关性，与本句结论相反，不能用 Consistent with。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"Parallel with 表「与……平行、并列发生」，强调两者同向并存，并未传达对立或反差；用在此处仍属逻辑方向不符。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Peculiar to 表「为某物所特有的」，例如 a disease peculiar to children，描述属性归属；与「记述对比新结论」的语境完全错位。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"evidence"},{"key":"B","text":"guidance"},{"key":"C","text":"implication"},{"key":"D","text":"source"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"13.","reason":"「未找到系统性证据表明 X 与 Y 相关」 线索是整句结构 no systematic __(13)__ was found that levels of productivity were related to changes in lighting——that-从句陈述的是有待验证的假说「产量与照明相关」，能与之搭配的是 evidence「证据」，整句意为「没找到系统性证据表明产量与照明相关」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"evidence 表「证据」，systematic evidence that ... 是「系统性证据表明……」的经典搭配，与「数据复检未发现产量受光照影响」的论证场景高度吻合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"guidance 表「指导、指引」，意指方法上的建议，与论证某结论是否成立无关；systematic guidance that 也不构成固定表达。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"implication 表「暗示、含义」，强调间接推论；研究语境里 was found 后多接「证据」而非「暗示」；且 systematic implication 罕用，不如 evidence 精准。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"source 表「来源、根源」，多接 of + 名词（the source of the problem），不能用 that-从句作同位语来说明命题内容，结构与语义均不符。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"disputable"},{"key":"B","text":"enlightening"},{"key":"C","text":"reliable"},{"key":"D","text":"misleading"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"14.","reason":"实验方式有缺陷→产生「误导性」解读 线索一是 peculiar way 已暗示问题；线索二是下文 a comparison with data for weeks when there was no experimentation showed that output always went up on Mondays——揭示真正的「周一惯性高产」机制，证明 P2 那种「察觉=改变行为」的解读其实是误读。所以应填 misleading「误导性的」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"disputable 表「有争议的、可被质疑的」，停留在「不确定」层面；但作者已经用数据推翻旧解读，远不止有争议而已，应是「误导性的」。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"enlightening 是「富有启发的」，褒义；但 P4 全段是要拆穿旧解读为误，褒义形容词与作者立场反向。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"reliable 是「可靠的」，褒义；与作者明确否定旧解读的立场冲突，且既然下文用数据证伪，就更谈不上「可靠」。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"misleading 意为「误导性的」，精准对应「实验方式特殊导致对所发生情况的误解」，并为 P4 后文的真因揭示铺垫，与全文复盘基调一致。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"In contrast"},{"key":"B","text":"For example"},{"key":"C","text":"In consequence"},{"key":"D","text":"As usual"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"15.","reason":"前句概括→本句给出具体做法 前句 the peculiar way of conducting the experiments may have led to __(14)__ interpretations of what happened 是抽象的「特殊做法导致误解」；本句 lighting was always changed on a Sunday 给出「特殊做法」的具体一例——总在周日改光线。这是典型的「概括→举例」关系，应填 For example。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"In contrast 表「与之相反」，前后句之间应有对立的两个对象/观点；但本句只是给前句一个具体例子，没有对照对象。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"For example 表「例如」，是「前句概括→后句具体例子」的标准标记；前句说做法特殊导致误读，本句举出「总在周日调光」这一具体做法作支撑，是教科书级的举例关系。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"In consequence 表「因此」，强调结果；但本句不是前句的结果，而是前句的具体例证，关系类别不同。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"As usual 是描述「按惯例发生」，无法体现「举例」关系；且作者在此并未强调「按惯例」，而是要揭示一个具体疏漏。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"duly"},{"key":"B","text":"accidentally"},{"key":"C","text":"unpredictably"},{"key":"D","text":"suddenly"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"16.","reason":"周一产量上升是「按惯例发生」 线索在后文 a comparison with data for weeks when there was no experimentation showed that output always went up on Mondays——「连没做实验的周也是周一产量总上升」，说明周一产量上升是规律性事件，不是意外，应填 duly「按期、如约、自然而然」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"duly 表「按预期、如约、恰如其分」，正对应后文 always went up on Mondays「总是在周一上升」的规律性，是作者强调这次也不例外的恰当副词。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"accidentally 表「偶然、意外」，与后文 always went up on Mondays 的规律性直接冲突。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"unpredictably 表「不可预测地」，但作者下文恰恰说每个周一都上升，可预测，副词指向相反。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"suddenly 表「突然」，关注「事件来得快」；这里作者要说的是「按惯例、可预期」的常态变化，而非突变。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"failed"},{"key":"B","text":"ceased"},{"key":"C","text":"started"},{"key":"D","text":"continued"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"17.","reason":"周一上升后接下来几天仍在上升 线索是前文 output __(16)__ rose「周一产量已上升」与后续 for the next couple of days「接下来几天」——两者用 and 串起来说明上升趋势在后续几天继续，应是 continued to rise。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"failed to rise 表「未能上升」，与上下文「接下来几天仍上升、之后才进入平台期」的描述完全相反。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"ceased to rise 表「停止上升」，但下文还提到 before __(20)__ a plateau and then slackening off 说明上升一直到达到平台才结束，并非立即停止。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"started to rise 表「开始上升」，但前半句 output rose 已说周一就上升了，再用 started 会和事实冲突，逻辑不连贯。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"continued to rise 表「继续上升」，正对应「周一已升，接下来几天仍在升」的并列描述，并与下一句 before __(20)__ a plateau and then slackening off 的「到达平台前一直上升」连成一气。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Therefore"},{"key":"B","text":"Furthermore"},{"key":"C","text":"However"},{"key":"D","text":"Meanwhile"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"18.","reason":"前文说「实验周周一上升似可归因于实验」→本句揭示其实「无实验周也升」 前文 output __(16)__ rose compared with the previous Saturday and __(17)__ to rise for the next couple of days 还在描述实验周内的产量上升，看似可归因实验；本句 a comparison with data for weeks when there was no experimentation showed that output always went up on Mondays 突然引入「无实验周也升」的对照，是一个推翻前面隐含归因的转折，应填 However。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"Therefore 表「因此」，若代入会变成「（因为周一上升数日）因此对照显示周一总上升」，因果链不成立；本质上后句是推翻前推断的新证据，不是推论结果。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"Furthermore 表「此外」，表示同方向加码；但本句以「无实验周也上升」的事实让前面的实验归因不成立，需要的是反差信号。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"However 表「然而」，正对应「前面看似归因实验→后面对照数据揭示并非如此」的转折逻辑，是 P4 真因揭示的关键标志词。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Meanwhile 表「同时、与此同时」，强调时间维度的并行；本句不是描述同时发生的事，而是给出反证证据，逻辑类别不符。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"attempted"},{"key":"B","text":"tended"},{"key":"C","text":"chose"},{"key":"D","text":"intended"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"19.","reason":"「不管怎样、工人每周头几天都更勤奋」是普遍倾向 线索是 Workers __(19)__ to be diligent for the first few days of the week in any case 中的 in any case「无论如何」，以及下半句 before __(20)__ a plateau and then slackening off 表明这是一种规律性的工作节律，描述的是一般倾向，对应 tend to do「倾向于」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"attempted 表「尝试」，带有「主动努力、且不一定成功」的色彩，与「客观规律性高产」的描述不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"tended 与 to 搭出 tend to do「倾向于做」，描述群体在某情境下普遍呈现的客观趋势，正契合「不管怎样、每周头几天工人都更勤奋」的规律性观察。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"chose 表「选择」，带主观决断意味；客观规律性现象更适合用 tended，不是 chose。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"intended 表「打算、意图」，强调主观规划；与统计现象「工人在前几天都更勤奋」不在同一描述维度。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"breaking"},{"key":"B","text":"climbing"},{"key":"C","text":"surpassing"},{"key":"D","text":"hitting"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"20.","reason":"「先上升→到达平台→再回落」的节奏 线索是上下文节奏：前面说工人头几天勤奋（产量上升），紧接 a plateau and then slackening off「达到平台然后松懈」——意为「先升到顶点然后回落」。「达到平台期」的英语标准说法是 hit a plateau。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"breaking a plateau 字面是「打破平台期」，本意是冲出停滞继续向上；与下文 slackening off「松懈」矛盾，且本身不是英语固定搭配。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"climbing 通常接 mountain/hill 等可被攀上的对象；climb a plateau 不构成固定表达，且方向意味「向上」，与「到达瓶颈」相反。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"surpassing 表「超越」，意味突破平台继续上升；但下文 slackening off 是松懈下降，因果链对不上。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"hitting 与 a plateau 构成 hit a plateau「触及平台期、达到瓶颈」的固定搭配，正对应「头几天升、之后触顶、然后松懈」的工作节奏。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-1","kind":"reading","title":"Text 1","textNo":1,"directions":"Directions: Read the following four texts. Answer the questions after each text by choosing A, B, C or D. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET . (40 points)","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 1","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-1","text":"Of all the changes that have taken place in English-language newspapers during the past quarter-century, perhaps the most far-reaching has been the inexorable decline in the scope and seriousness of their arts coverage."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-2","text":"It is difficult to the point of impossibility for the average reader under the age of forty to imagine a time when high-quality arts criticism could be found in most big-city newspapers. Yet a considerable number of the most significant collections of criticism published in the 20th century consisted in large part of newspaper reviews. To read such books today is to marvel at the fact that their learned contents were once deemed suitable for publication in general-circulation dailies."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-3","text":"We are even farther removed from the unfocused newspaper reviews published in England between the turn of the 20th century and the eve of World War II, at a time when newsprint was dirt-cheap and stylish arts criticism was considered an ornament to the publications in which it appeared. In those far-off days, it was taken for granted that the critics of major papers would write in detail and at length about the events they covered. Theirs was a serious business, and even those reviewers who wore their learning lightly, like George Bernard Shaw and Ernest Newman, could be trusted to know what they were about. These men believed in journalism as a calling, and were proud to be published in the daily press. \"So few authors have brains enough or literary gift enough to keep their own end up in journalism,\" Newman wrote, \"that I am tempted to define 'journalism' as 'a term of contempt applied by writers who are not read to writers who are'.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-4","text":"Unfortunately, these critics are virtually forgotten. Neville Cardus, who wrote for the Manchester Guardian from 1917 until shortly before his death in 1975, is now known solely as a writer of essays on the game of cricket. During his lifetime, though, he was also one of England's foremost classical-music critics, and a stylist so widely admired that his Autobiography (1947) became a best-seller. He was knighted in 1967, the first music critic to be so honored. Yet only one of his books is now in print, and his vast body of writings on music is unknown save to specialists."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-5","text":"Is there any chance that Cardus's criticism will enjoy a revival? The prospect seems remote. Journalistic tastes had changed long before his death, and postmodern readers have little use for the richly upholstered Vicwardian prose in which he specialized. Moreover, the amateur tradition in music criticism has been in headlong retreat."}]},"questions":[{"n":21,"stem":"It is indicated in Paragraphs 1 and 2 that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"arts criticism has disappeared from big-city newspapers."},{"key":"B","text":"English-language newspapers used to carry more arts reviews."},{"key":"C","text":"high-quality newspapers retain a large body of readers."},{"key":"D","text":"young readers doubt the suitability of criticism on dailies."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"第1段和第2段表明____","choicesZh":{"A":"艺术批评已从大城市报纸中消失。","B":"英语报纸过去刊载更多艺术评论。","C":"高质量报纸保有大量读者群。","D":"年轻读者质疑日报上批评的适宜性。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 It is indicated in Paragraphs 1 and 2 用 indicated 而非 imply/infer，要求答案是原文已经写出来的内容，不需要推。","parse":"句子主干 It is indicated in Paragraphs 1 and 2 that ____，形式主语 it + 被动 is indicated + that 从句留白。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"It is difficult to the point of impossibility for the average reader under the age of forty to imagine a time when high-quality arts criticism could be found in most big-city newspapers.","locateZh":"对于一个 40 岁以下的普通读者而言，几乎不可能想象曾经有一个时代，大多数大城市报纸上都能找到高质量的艺术评论。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"arts criticism has disappeared from big-city newspapers 把原文的 decline 拔高成 disappeared，但 decline in the scope and seriousness 仅说下降，并未说完全消失。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"B 项同时承接了 P1 的 decline 和 P2 的 a time when... could be found 这条今昔对比主线，是定位句最克制的客观转述。","pairs":[{"orig":"a time when high-quality arts criticism could be found in most big-city newspapers","opt":"English-language newspapers used to carry more arts reviews"},{"orig":"the inexorable decline in the scope and seriousness of their arts coverage","opt":"more arts reviews"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"high-quality newspapers retain a large body of readers 的话题是 readers 数量，而原文谈的是 arts criticism 的多少与质量。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"young readers doubt the suitability of criticism on dailies 把'年轻读者无法想象'歪曲成'年轻读者怀疑评论是否合适'。原文 difficult... to imagine 是不能想象，were once deemed suitable 的 suitable 是作者对过去的感慨，不是年轻读者的态度。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":22,"stem":"Newspaper reviews in England before World War II were characterized by____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"free themes."},{"key":"B","text":"casual style."},{"key":"C","text":"elaborate layout."},{"key":"D","text":"radical viewpoints."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"二战前英国的报纸评论具有____的特点","choicesZh":{"A":"自由的主题。","B":"随意的风格。","C":"精心设计的版面。","D":"激进的观点。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 characterized by ____ 问 reviews 的具体特征，定位即可，不需推断。","parse":"Newspaper reviews in England before World War II were characterized by ____，主干 reviews were characterized by ___；两个介词短语 in England / before World War II 是后置修饰主语。结构清晰。","locateEn":"We are even farther removed from the unfocused newspaper reviews published in England between the turn of the 20th century and the eve of World War II, at a time when newsprint was dirt-cheap and stylish arts criticism was considered an ornament to the publications in which it appeared. In those far-off days, it was taken for granted that the critics of major papers would write in detail and at length about the events they covered.","locateZh":"我们距离 20 世纪初到二战前夕英国报纸上那些散漫不聚焦的评论更加遥远；那时候新闻纸便宜得离谱，有风格的艺术评论被视为刊登它的出版物的一种装饰。在那段久远的日子里，主要报纸的评论家会就所报道的事件写得详尽冗长，这是被视为理所当然的。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"四个选项中只有 A 项对应 unfocused 这一原文紧贴本体的形容词，其余选项都越出了定位句的描述。","pairs":[{"orig":"the unfocused newspaper reviews","opt":"free themes"},{"orig":"write in detail and at length about the events they covered","opt":"free themes"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"casual style 把 stylish arts criticism 偷换成'随意的风格'，stylish 指有风格/讲究风格的，casual 指随便、不讲究，方向相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"elaborate layout 指'精致的版面布局'，但 an ornament to the publications 谈的是评论本身是出版物的装饰，并非排版精致；layout 在原文没有任何依据。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"radical viewpoints 指激进观点，但 P3 全段只谈评论的范围、风格、长度，未提及评论家的观点偏向。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":23,"stem":"Which of the following would Shaw and Newman most probably agree on?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is writers' duty to fulfill journalistic goals."},{"key":"B","text":"It is contemptible for writers to be journalists."},{"key":"C","text":"Writers are likely to be tempted into journalism."},{"key":"D","text":"Not all writers are capable of journalistic writing."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"推断题","stemZh":"Shaw和Newman最可能在以下哪一点上达成一致?","choicesZh":{"A":"履行新闻目标是作家的职责。","B":"作家从事新闻工作是可鄙的。","C":"作家很可能受诱惑而从事新闻工作。","D":"并非所有作家都有能力从事新闻写作。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 Which of the following would Shaw and Newman most probably agree on? 含 most probably，要求基于原文做一步合理推断。","parse":"Which of the following would Shaw and Newman most probably agree on?，疑问主语 Which + 情态动词 would + 主语 Shaw and Newman + 谓语 agree on。无难点。","locateEn":"\"So few authors have brains enough or literary gift enough to keep their own end up in journalism,\" Newman wrote, \"that I am tempted to define 'journalism' as 'a term of contempt applied by writers who are not read to writers who are\".","locateZh":"Newman 写道：'极少有作家具备足够的头脑或文学才能在新闻业里撑住自己的水准，以致我都想把 journalism 一词定义为：那些没人读的作家用来鄙夷那些有人读的作家时所用的轻蔑之辞。'","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"It is writers' duty to fulfill journalistic goals 把 These men believed in journalism as a calling 的'把新闻当作天职'拔高成'所有作家都有义务做新闻'；believed in 与 duty 不等值。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"It is contemptible for writers to be journalists 直陈'作家做新闻是可耻的'，但 a term of contempt applied by writers who are not read to writers who are 的语义恰恰相反——是没人读的作家用 'journalism' 来贬低有人读的作家，作者揭这个事实正是反讽。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Writers are likely to be tempted into journalism 把 I am tempted to define 的 tempted 偷换成'被引入新闻业的诱惑'。原文 tempted 的对象是 to define（想下定义），不是'被吸引去做新闻'；且主语是 I（Newman 本人），不是 writers 整体。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Newman 是直接说话者；Shaw 与 Newman 同在 like George Bernard Shaw and Ernest Newman, could be trusted to know what they were about 一句中被并列为'懂行的评论家'，所以 Newman 这句感慨可视为他们共享的从业经验——并非所有作家都能写好新闻。","pairs":[{"orig":"So few authors have brains enough or literary gift enough to keep their own end up in journalism","opt":"Not all writers are capable of journalistic writing"}]}}}}},{"n":24,"stem":"What can be learned about Cardus according to the last two paragraphs?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"His music criticism may not appeal to readers today."},{"key":"B","text":"His reputation as a music critic has long been in dispute."},{"key":"C","text":"His style caters largely to modern specialists."},{"key":"D","text":"His writings fail to follow the amateur tradition."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"推断题","stemZh":"根据最后两段,关于Cardus可以了解到什么?","choicesZh":{"A":"他的音乐批评可能不会吸引今天的读者。","B":"他作为音乐批评家的声誉长期存在争议。","C":"他的风格主要迎合现代专业人士。","D":"他的作品未能遵循业余传统。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 What can be learned about Cardus according to the last two paragraphs? 的 can be learned 暗示要从原文事实再走一步得到结论。","parse":"What can be learned about Cardus according to the last two paragraphs?，疑问代词 What + 情态 can + 被动 be learned + 介短 about Cardus + according to 介短作状语；无难点。","locateEn":"Journalistic tastes had changed long before his death, and postmodern readers have little use for the richly upholstered Vicwardian prose in which he specialized. Moreover, the amateur tradition in music criticism has been in headlong retreat.","locateZh":"新闻趣味在他去世之前早就变了，今天的后现代读者已经没怎么用得上他所擅长的那种繁复华丽的维多利亚-爱德华时代散文；此外，音乐评论中的'业余传统'也在节节败退。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"A 项把作者明确给出的'今天读者用不上'的判断换成委婉的 may not appeal to readers today，未拔高、未偏移；这正是推断题应有的克制。","pairs":[{"orig":"postmodern readers have little use for the richly upholstered Vicwardian prose in which he specialized","opt":"His music criticism may not appeal to readers today"},{"orig":"Is there any chance that Cardus's criticism will enjoy a revival? The prospect seems remote.","opt":"His music criticism may not appeal to readers today"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"His reputation as a music critic has long been in dispute 称其声誉长期有争议，但 P4 显示 Cardus 生前被 widely admired、1967 年首位被封爵的乐评家；今天则是 unknown save to specialists（被遗忘），不是被争议。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"His style caters largely to modern specialists 称其文风迎合现代专家，但 his vast body of writings on music is unknown save to specialists 与 postmodern readers have little use for the richly upholstered Vicwardian prose 合起来说的是：今天只有专家还读他，并不是他刻意去迎合现代专家——caters to 是有意取悦，与原文'被动地只剩专家会读'方向相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"His writings fail to follow the amateur tradition 说他没有遵循业余传统；但 the amateur tradition in music criticism has been in headlong retreat 谈的是这一传统整体在退潮，并未说 Cardus 个人偏离它，反而 P4 暗示他正属于这一传统的代表。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":25,"stem":"What would be the best title for the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Newspapers of the Good Old Days"},{"key":"B","text":"The Lost Horizon in Newspapers"},{"key":"C","text":"Mournful Decline of Journalism"},{"key":"D","text":"Prominent Critics in Memory"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"这篇文章的最佳标题是什么?","choicesZh":{"A":"昔日美好时光的报纸","B":"报纸中失落的视野","C":"新闻业的悲哀衰落","D":"记忆中的杰出批评家"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 What would be the best title for the text? 中 best title 直指文章主旨题。","parse":"What would be the best title for the text?，主语 What + would be + 表语 the best title + 介短 for the text。无难点。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Newspapers of the Good Old Days 给人怀旧温情感，但全文核心是哀其'衰退/失落'，而非赞美'好时光'；且只覆盖 P3 的回忆，遗漏 P1 的衰退主线。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"B 项既能覆盖 P1 的总论 decline，也能呼应 P5 的不可复兴，是唯一一个能贯穿所有区间的标题。","pairs":[{"orig":"the inexorable decline in the scope and seriousness of their arts coverage","opt":"The Lost Horizon in Newspapers"},{"orig":"The prospect seems remote","opt":"The Lost Horizon in Newspapers"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Mournful Decline of Journalism 哀叹的是整个新闻业的衰落，但原文只谈 arts coverage 这一块的衰退，并非整个 journalism；范围被无端放大。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Prominent Critics in Memory 只对应 P4 中 Neville Cardus 这类被遗忘的评论家个案，没法承担 P1 的总论与 P2 的今昔对比；个案当主旨即以偏概全。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-2","kind":"reading","title":"Text 2","textNo":2,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 2","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-1","text":"Over the past decade, thousands of patents have been granted for what are called business methods. Amazon.com received one for its \"one-click\" online payment system. Merrill Lynch got legal protection for an asset allocation strategy. One inventor patented a technique for lifting a box."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-2","text":"Now the nation's top patent court appears completely ready to scale back on business-method patents, which have been controversial ever since they were first authorized 10 years ago. In a move that has intellectual-property lawyers abuzz, the U.S. Court of Appeals for the Federal Circuit said it would use a particular case to conduct a broad review of business-method patents. In re Bilski, as the case is known, is \"a very big deal,\" says Dennis D. Crouch of the University of Missouri School of Law. It \"has the potential to eliminate an entire class of patents.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-3","text":"Curbs on business-method claims would be a dramatic about-face, because it was the Federal Circuit itself that introduced such patents with its 1998 decision in the so-called State Street Bank case, approving a patent on a way of pooling mutual-fund assets. That ruling produced an explosion in business-method patent filings, initially by emerging Internet companies trying to stake out exclusive rights to specific types of online transactions. Later, more established companies raced to add such patents to their files, if only as a defensive move against rivals that might beat them to the punch. In 2005, IBM noted in a court filing that it had been issued more than 300 business-method patents, despite the fact that it questioned the legal basis for granting them. Similarly, some Wall Street investment firms armed themselves with patents for financial products, even as they took positions in court cases opposing the practice."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-4","text":"The Bilski case involves a claimed patent on a method for hedging risk in the energy market. The Federal Circuit issued an unusual order stating that the case would be heard by all 12 of the court's judges, rather than a typical panel of three, and that one issue it wants to evaluate is whether it should \"reconsider\" its State Street Bank ruling."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-5","text":"The Federal Circuit's action comes in the wake of a series of recent decisions by the Supreme Court that have narrowed the scope of protections for patent holders. Last April, for example, the justices signaled that too many patents were being upheld for \"inventions\" that are obvious. The judges on the Federal Circuit are \"reacting to the anti-patent trend at the Supreme Court,\" says Harold C. Wegner, a patent attorney and professor at George Washington University Law School."}]},"questions":[{"n":26,"stem":"Business-method patents have recently aroused concern because of____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"their limited value to businesses."},{"key":"B","text":"their connection with asset allocation."},{"key":"C","text":"the possible restriction on their granting."},{"key":"D","text":"the controversy over their authorization."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"商业方法专利最近引起关注是因为____","choicesZh":{"A":"它们对企业的价值有限。","B":"它们与资产配置的联系。","C":"对其授予可能存在的限制。","D":"围绕其授权的争议。"},"analysis":{"type":"Business-method patents have recently aroused concern because of 用 because of 直接索要 \"引起担忧的原因\"，是典型的原因型细节题。","parse":"Business-method patents have recently aroused concern because of____ 是一个待补全陈述句，主干是 \"Business-method patents have aroused concern\"，recently 是时间状语，because of 引出原因，空格处填名词性成分。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Now the nation's top patent court appears completely ready to scale back on business-method patents, which have been controversial ever since they were first authorized 10 years ago.","locateZh":"如今，全国最高的专利法院似乎已完全准备好收紧商业方法专利——自十年前首次获准以来，这类专利就一直争议不断。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"their limited value to businesses 在原文中没有任何依据——文章只字未提此类专利对企业 \"价值有限\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Merrill Lynch got legal protection for an asset allocation strategy 只是第 1 段举的一个案例，意在说明商业方法专利的存在，与 \"recently aroused concern 的原因\" 无关。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判 \"准备收紧授予\" 与 the possible restriction on their granting 在语义上完全对应，故选 C。","pairs":[{"orig":"ready to scale back on business-method patents","opt":"the possible restriction on their granting"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 which have been controversial ever since they were first authorized 10 years ago 说的是 \"自十年前授予以来一直有争议\"，是背景性长期争议；题干问的是 recently aroused concern 的近期原因，不是十年前授予时的争议。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":27,"stem":"Which of the following is true of the Bilski case?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Its ruling complies with the court decisions."},{"key":"B","text":"It involves a very big business transaction."},{"key":"C","text":"It has been dismissed by the Federal Circuit."},{"key":"D","text":"It may change the legal practices in the U.S."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"关于Bilski案,下列哪项是正确的?","choicesZh":{"A":"其裁决符合法院判决。","B":"它涉及一项非常大的商业交易。","C":"它已被联邦巡回法院驳回。","D":"它可能改变美国的法律实践。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following is true of the Bilski case 要在四项中挑出与原文事实一致的一项，属于 which-is-true 型细节题。","parse":"Which of the following is true of the Bilski case? 是疑问句，true of X 意为 \"关于 X 的真实情况\"。结构直白，无陷阱。","locateEn":"The Federal Circuit issued an unusual order stating that the case would be heard by all 12 of the court's judges, rather than a typical panel of three, and that one issue it wants to evaluate is whether it should \"reconsider\" its State Street Bank ruling.","locateZh":"联邦巡回上诉法院发出一项不同寻常的命令，称此案将由该院全部 12 名法官共同审理，而不是惯常的三人合议庭；该院想评估的议题之一，是是否应 \"重新审视 \" 当年的 State Street Bank 判例。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"The Federal Circuit's action comes in the wake of a series of recent decisions by the Supreme Court that have narrowed the scope of protections for patent holders 表明 Bilski 案是 \"顺应\" 最高法院的反专利趋势，但 Its ruling complies with the court decisions 中的 \"ruling\" 暗指 Bilski 案已有裁决——而原文显示该案尚在审理阶段，根本谈不上 ruling 与法院判决相符。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文 The Bilski case involves a claimed patent on a method for hedging risk in the energy market 涉及的是 \"一种能源市场对冲风险方法的专利\"，是一项技术性专利申请；选项 It involves a very big business transaction（涉及一笔重大商业交易）把 \"对一项方法的专利申请 \" 偷换成了 \"重大商业交易\"。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 The Federal Circuit issued an unusual order stating that the case would be heard by all 12 of the court's judges 明确指出该案将由全院 12 名法官审理，与 It has been dismissed by the Federal Circuit（已被驳回）完全相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"全院审 + 明确要重审先例 + 有可能 \"消除整类专利\"，与 may change the legal practices in the U.S. 完全对位，故选 D。","pairs":[{"orig":"whether it should \"reconsider\" its State Street Bank ruling","opt":"It may change the legal practices in the U.S."}]}}}}},{"n":28,"stem":"The word \"about-face\" (Line 1, Para. 3) most probably means____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"loss of goodwill."},{"key":"B","text":"increase of hostility."},{"key":"C","text":"change of attitude."},{"key":"D","text":"enhancement of dignity."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"第三段第一行中\"about-face\"一词最可能的意思是____","choicesZh":{"A":"失去善意。","B":"敌意增加。","C":"态度转变。","D":"尊严提升。"},"analysis":{"type":"The word \"about-face\" (Line 1, Para. 3) most probably means 直接问某词的含义，是典型词义题。","parse":"The word \"about-face\" (Line 1, Para. 3) most probably means____ 是待补全陈述句，most probably 表示 \"最可能\"，提示该词非字面、需结合语境推断。","locateEn":"Curbs on business-method claims would be a dramatic about-face, because it was the Federal Circuit itself that introduced such patents with its 1998 decision in the so-called State Street Bank case, approving a patent on a way of pooling mutual-fund assets.","locateZh":"对商业方法主张加以限制，将是一次戏剧性的 about-face（180 度转向），因为正是 Federal Circuit 自己在 1998 年的所谓 State Street Bank 案中以判决引入了此类专利，批准了一种汇集共同基金资产的方法专利。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"loss of goodwill（信誉受损）在原文没有任何对应——文章只描述法院前后立场对立，并未评价这会让法院 \"丢掉信誉\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"increase of hostility（敌意增加）原文亦无对应——法院只是收紧专利，并未对申请人 \"敌意增加\"。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"同一主体先后做出对立行为，对应的中文释义就是 \"态度大转弯\"，与 change of attitude 等值，故选 C。","pairs":[{"orig":"Curbs on business-method claims would be a dramatic about-face, because it was the Federal Circuit itself that introduced such patents","opt":"change of attitude"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"enhancement of dignity（尊严提升）与原文情感色彩相反——原文 dramatic about-face 隐含 \"自己打自己脸\" 的微妙否定意味，绝非 \"尊严提升\"。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":29,"stem":"We learn from the last two paragraphs that business-method patents____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"are immune to legal challenges."},{"key":"B","text":"are often unnecessarily issued."},{"key":"C","text":"lower the esteem for patent holders."},{"key":"D","text":"increase the incidence of risks."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从最后两段我们了解到商业方法专利____","choicesZh":{"A":"不受法律质疑的影响。","B":"经常被不必要地授予。","C":"降低了对专利持有人的尊重。","D":"增加了风险发生率。"},"analysis":{"type":"We learn from the last two paragraphs that 用 \"we learn\"，要求从段落整体推出未明说但有据的结论，是推断题。","parse":"We learn from the last two paragraphs that business-method patents____ 是 we learn from X that Y 结构，从 X 里学到 Y 的内容；空格填对 business-method patents 的判断。","locateEn":"Last April, for example, the justices signaled that too many patents were being upheld for \"inventions\" that are obvious.","locateZh":"比如，去年四月，大法官们便发出信号：太多专利被授予给了那些其实显而易见的所谓 \"发明 \"。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文第 4、5 段恰恰展示了商业方法专利正在面临 In re Bilski 案的全院审查与最高法院反专利潮的双重冲击，are immune to legal challenges（不受法律挑战）与原文完全相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"推断结论\"本不该发却被发出去了\" 完全等于 are often unnecessarily issued，故选 B。","pairs":[{"orig":"too many patents were being upheld for \"inventions\" that are obvious","opt":"are often unnecessarily issued"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文未对 \"专利持有人的社会声望（esteem for patent holders）\" 作任何评价；lower the esteem for patent holders 是凭空捏造。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 The Bilski case involves a claimed patent on a method for hedging risk in the energy market 中的 risk 是 \"对冲风险的方法\" 中的对冲对象，并不是说商业方法专利本身 \"增加了风险发生率\"；选项偷换了 risk 的所指。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":30,"stem":"Which of the following would be the subject of the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A looming threat to business-method patents."},{"key":"B","text":"Protection for business-method patent holders."},{"key":"C","text":"A legal case regarding business-method patents."},{"key":"D","text":"A prevailing trend against business-method patents."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"下列哪项会是本文的主题?","choicesZh":{"A":"商业方法专利面临的迫在眉睫的威胁。","B":"对商业方法专利持有人的保护。","C":"一起关于商业方法专利的法律案件。","D":"反对商业方法专利的普遍趋势。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following would be the subject of the text 直接索要 the subject of the text（全文主题），是标准主旨题。","parse":"Which of the following would be the subject of the text? 是疑问句，would be 是虚拟语气表 \"最适合作\"，subject 在此意为 \"主题\"。结构无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"主线的一句话浓缩就是 \"对商业方法专利的逼近威胁\"，与 A looming threat to business-method patents. 完全等值，故选 A。","pairs":[{"orig":"ready to scale back on business-method patents","opt":"A looming threat to business-method patents."},{"orig":"It \"has the potential to eliminate an entire class of patents.\"","opt":"A looming threat to business-method patents."}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"全文是讲 business-method patent holders 正面临收紧与挑战，Protection for business-method patent holders. 反其道而行——把 \"威胁\" 写成 \"保护\"，与主线情感色彩相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"P4 的 The Bilski case involves a claimed patent on a method for hedging risk in the energy market 只是全文的一个支撑案例，A legal case regarding business-method patents. 把这一案例抬升为全文主题，忽略了第 1、2、3、5 段的铺垫与升华。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"A prevailing trend against business-method patents. 听上去与 A 相近，但 \"prevailing trend（已盛行的趋势）\" 与原文表述不符——原文强调的是 Federal Circuit 借 Bilski \"appears completely ready to scale back\"（即将出手的逼近性威胁）、是动作前夕；prevailing trend 把 \"未起势 \" 说成 \"已成势\"。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-3","kind":"reading","title":"Text 3","textNo":3,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 3","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-1","text":"In his book The Tipping Point, Malcolm Gladwell argues that \"social epidemics\" are driven in large part by the actions of a tiny minority of special individuals, often called influentials, who are unusually informed, persuasive, or well connected. The idea is intuitively compelling, but it doesn't explain how ideas actually spread."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-2","text":"The supposed importance of influentials derives from a plausible-sounding but largely untested theory called the \"two-step flow of communication\": Information flows from the media to the influentials and from them to everyone else. Marketers have embraced the two-step flow because it suggests that if they can just find and influence the influentials, those select people will do most of the work for them. The theory also seems to explain the sudden and unexpected popularity of certain looks, brands, or neighborhoods. In many such cases, a cursory search for causes finds that some small group of people was wearing, promoting, or developing whatever it is before anyone else paid attention. Anecdotal evidence of this kind fits nicely with the idea that only certain special people can drive trends."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-3","text":"In their recent work, however, some researchers have come up with the finding that influentials have far less impact on social epidemics than is generally supposed. In fact, they don't seem to be required at all."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-4","text":"The researchers' argument stems from a simple observation about social influence: With the exception of a few celebrities like Oprah Winfrey – whose outsize presence is primarily a function of media, not interpersonal, influence – even the most influential members of a population simply don't interact with that many others. Yet it is precisely these non-celebrity influentials who, according to the two-step-flow theory, are supposed to drive social epidemics, by influencing their friends and colleagues directly. For a social epidemic to occur, however, each person so affected must then influence his or her own acquaintances, who must in turn influence theirs, and so on; and just how many others pay attention to each of these people has little to do with the initial influential. If people in the network just two degrees removed from the initial influential prove resistant, for example, the cascade of change won't propagate very far or affect many people."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-5","text":"Building on this basic truth about interpersonal influence, the researchers studied the dynamics of social influence by conducting thousands of computer simulations of populations, manipulating a number of variables relating to people's ability to influence others and their tendency to be influenced. They found that the principal requirement for what is called \"global cascades\" – the widespread propagation of influence through networks – is the presence not of a few influentials but, rather, of a critical mass of easily influenced people."}]},"questions":[{"n":31,"stem":"By citing the book The Tipping Point, the author intends to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"analyze the consequences of social epidemics."},{"key":"B","text":"discuss influentials' function in spreading ideas."},{"key":"C","text":"exemplify people's intuitive response to social epidemics."},{"key":"D","text":"describe the essential characteristics of influentials."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"作者引用《引爆点》一书旨在____","choicesZh":{"A":"分析社会流行的后果。","B":"讨论影响者在传播思想中的作用。","C":"例证人们对社会流行的直觉反应。","D":"描述影响者的基本特征。"},"analysis":{"type":"By citing the book The Tipping Point, the author intends to 明确问\"通过引用某书，作者意图是\"，这是典型的例证/引用目的题。","parse":"By citing the book The Tipping Point, the author intends to____ 主干是 the author intends to + 选项动词原形；By citing… 是方式状语，限定意图发生的场合，不是宾语，别把宾语理解成 the book。","locateEn":"In his book The Tipping Point, Malcolm Gladwell argues that \"social epidemics\" are driven in large part by the actions of a tiny minority of special individuals, often called influentials, who are unusually informed, persuasive, or well connected. The idea is intuitively compelling, but it doesn't explain how ideas actually spread.","locateZh":"Gladwell 在《引爆点》中主张：\"社会流行\"主要由一小撮特殊个体（influentials，意为有影响力者）的行动驱动，这些人见多识广、有说服力、人脉广。这个想法直觉上很有吸引力，但它解释不了思想到底是怎么传播开的。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"A 项把讨论对象换成 consequences of social epidemics（社会流行的后果），但作者全文聚焦的是\"原因/驱动机制\"——influentials 是不是驱动力，与\"后果\"无关。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判要的是\"借书引入议题\"，B 的 discuss influentials' function in spreading ideas 既点出讨论对象（influentials 在传播中的作用），又用 discuss 这一中性词承接作者后文的反驳——完全匹配。","pairs":[{"orig":"driven in large part by the actions of a tiny minority of special individuals, often called influentials","opt":"influentials' function in spreading ideas"},{"orig":"it doesn't explain how ideas actually spread","opt":"discuss"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"C 项 exemplify people's intuitive response to social epidemics 抓的是 intuitively compelling 一词，但 intuitively compelling 是作者对 Gladwell 想法的评价，不是作者想\"举例说明 people's intuitive response\"——这本书没有被用作\"直觉反应\"的例证。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"D 项 describe the essential characteristics of influentials 把引此书的目的说成\"描述 influentials 的本质特征\"。原文虽有 unusually informed, persuasive, or well connected 几个特征，但作者引此书的目的不是介绍 influentials 是什么人，而是要质疑\"他们到底有没有那么大作用\"。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":32,"stem":"The author suggests that the \"two-step-flow theory\" ____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"serves as a solution to marketing problems."},{"key":"B","text":"has helped explain certain prevalent trends."},{"key":"C","text":"has won support from influentials."},{"key":"D","text":"requires solid evidence for its validity."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"推断题","stemZh":"作者认为\"两级传播理论\"____","choicesZh":{"A":"可作为营销问题的解决方案。","B":"有助于解释某些流行趋势。","C":"赢得了影响者的支持。","D":"需要可靠证据来证明其有效性。"},"analysis":{"type":"The author suggests that 中的 suggests 表明问的不是原文直说的话，而是作者通过文本暗示的态度/判断。","parse":"The author suggests that the \"two-step-flow theory\" ____ 是带宾语从句的不完整句，that 从句的谓语就是四个选项，选项要能与从句主语 the two-step-flow theory 在语法上接得上。","locateEn":"The supposed importance of influentials derives from a plausible-sounding but largely untested theory called the \"two-step flow of communication\".","locateZh":"influentials 所谓的重要性，源自一种听上去合理但在很大程度上未经检验的理论，被称为\"两级传播\"理论。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"A 项 serves as a solution to marketing problems。原文 Marketers have embraced the two-step flow 只是说营销者\"拥抱\"该理论，并未说它真能\"解决\"营销问题——拥抱≠解决。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"B 项 has helped explain certain prevalent trends。原文 The theory also seems to explain the sudden and unexpected popularity——seems to explain（似乎能解释），核心限定词 seems 表明作者并不认同它真的解释了，B 项把 seems 偷换成 has helped explain。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"C 项 has won support from influentials。文章只说营销者（marketers）拥抱该理论，从未提到 influentials 本身\"支持\"该理论——influentials 在文中是被研究的对象，不是支持者。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判要的是\"该理论缺乏证据/需要证据\"，D 的 requires solid evidence for its validity 恰好是 largely untested 的换说法——同义改写关系最稳，是答案。","pairs":[{"orig":"largely untested","opt":"requires solid evidence for its validity"},{"orig":"plausible-sounding but largely untested","opt":"requires solid evidence for its validity"}]}}}}},{"n":33,"stem":"What the researchers have observed recently shows that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the power of influence goes with social interactions."},{"key":"B","text":"interpersonal links can be enhanced through the media."},{"key":"C","text":"influentials have more channels to reach the public."},{"key":"D","text":"most celebrities enjoy wide media attention."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"研究人员最近观察到的现象表明____","choicesZh":{"A":"影响力伴随社会互动而产生。","B":"人际联系可以通过媒体得到加强。","C":"影响者有更多渠道接触公众。","D":"大多数名人享有广泛的媒体关注。"},"analysis":{"type":"What the researchers have observed recently shows that____ 问\"研究者观察到的事实显示什么\"，要求对原文研究发现做客观转述。","parse":"What the researchers have observed recently shows that____ 主句是 What…shows that____，What 引导的主语从句作 shows 的主语；shows 后才是答案位，别把\"researchers observed\"的内容当成答案，要看\"该观察揭示了什么\"。","locateEn":"In their recent work, however, some researchers have come up with the finding that influentials have far less impact on social epidemics than is generally supposed.","locateZh":"然而，在近期的研究中，一些研究者得出了一个发现：有影响力者对社会流行的影响，远比人们通常以为的要小。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"研究者的发现是\"影响力的大小 = 人际互动的范围\"，A 用 goes with 把这层依存关系直白说出来——与定位句的论证完全契合。","pairs":[{"orig":"even the most influential members of a population simply don't interact with that many others","opt":"the power of influence goes with social interactions"},{"orig":"whose outsize presence is primarily a function of media, not interpersonal, influence","opt":"social interactions"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"B 项 interpersonal links can be enhanced through the media。原文是\"媒体绕过人际链条放大名人影响\"（outsize presence is primarily a function of media, not interpersonal），不是说\"媒体增强了人际链条\"——B 把媒体和人际的关系彻底颠倒。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"C 项 influentials have more channels to reach the public。研究者的发现恰恰相反——influentials 接触的人不多。原文从未涉及\"渠道多少\"的话题，C 凭空给 influentials 添加了\"传播渠道更多\"的属性。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"D 项 most celebrities enjoy wide media attention。原文里 Oprah 是被作为\"特例\"提及（With the exception of a few celebrities like Oprah Winfrey），且范围是 a few celebrities，不是 most celebrities；D 把例外当主张、把\"少数\"夸成\"大多数\"。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":34,"stem":"The underlined phrase \"these people\" in Paragraph 4 refers to the ones who____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"stay outside the network of social influence."},{"key":"B","text":"have little contact with the source of influence."},{"key":"C","text":"are influenced and then influence others."},{"key":"D","text":"are influenced by the initial influential."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"第4段中带下划线的短语\"这些人\"指的是那些____的人","choicesZh":{"A":"处于社会影响网络之外。","B":"与影响源接触很少。","C":"受到影响然后影响他人。","D":"受到最初影响者的影响。"},"analysis":{"type":"The underlined phrase \"these people\" in Paragraph 4 refers to the ones who____ 问划线短语指代的对象，是典型的代词/短语指代题，归词义句意类。","parse":"The underlined phrase \"these people\" in Paragraph 4 refers to the ones who____ 主干 the phrase refers to the ones；who 引导定语从句修饰 the ones，选项要能完整接 who，是\"那些……的人\"。","locateEn":"For a social epidemic to occur, however, each person so affected must then influence his or her own acquaintances, who must in turn influence theirs, and so on; and just how many others pay attention to each of these people has little to do with the initial influential.","locateZh":"然而要让社会流行真正发生，每个被影响的人必须接着去影响自己的熟人，这些熟人又必须去影响他们的熟人，如此层层下去；而每一环上的这些人能吸引多少其他人的关注，跟最初那个 influential 已经没什么关系了。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"A 项 stay outside the network of social influence。these people 恰恰在网络内部、是传播链上的一环，A 把他们说成\"在社会影响网络之外\"，与原文相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"B 项 have little contact with the source of influence。these people 是传播链中的每一环，他们自己\"被影响\"过——也就是直接接触过上游的影响源，不是\"与影响源接触少\"。B 把\"被影响\"误读为\"几乎没接触\"。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判要的就是\"被影响且接着影响他人\"的双重身份，C 用 are influenced and then influence others 一句把两动作完整说出来——其他选项要么只说一半，要么完全偏题。","pairs":[{"orig":"each person so affected must then influence his or her own acquaintances","opt":"are influenced and then influence others"},{"orig":"who must in turn influence theirs, and so on","opt":"and then influence others"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"D 项 are influenced by the initial influential。these people 确实被影响过，但定位句强调的是他们\"继续把影响传下去\"这一动作——D 只覆盖\"被影响\"的一半，丢掉了\"再去影响他人\"这一另一半。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":35,"stem":"What is the essential element in the dynamics of social influence?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The eagerness to be accepted."},{"key":"B","text":"The impulse to influence others."},{"key":"C","text":"The readiness to be influenced."},{"key":"D","text":"The inclination to rely on others."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"社会影响动态中的关键要素是什么?","choicesZh":{"A":"渴望被接纳。","B":"影响他人的冲动。","C":"乐于接受影响。","D":"依赖他人的倾向。"},"analysis":{"type":"What is the essential element in the dynamics of social influence? 用 What is 直接问事实性结论，是对末段研究结论的细节定位。","parse":"What is the essential element in the dynamics of social influence? 主干 What is the essential element；in the dynamics of social influence 是后置介词短语，限定 element 所属的领域，不要把它当成答案的一部分。","locateEn":"They found that the principal requirement for what is called \"global cascades\" – the widespread propagation of influence through networks – is the presence not of a few influentials but, rather, of a critical mass of easily influenced people.","locateZh":"他们发现，所谓\"全局级传播\"——也就是影响力在网络中广泛扩散——的首要条件，不是有少数 influentials 的存在，而是有一批数量足够的、易被影响的人。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"A 项 The eagerness to be accepted。原文说的是 easily influenced（容易被影响），不是 eager to be accepted（渴望被接纳）——\"被影响\"和\"被接纳\"是两件事，A 偷换了核心属性。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"B 项 The impulse to influence others。原文强调的是\"被影响的属性\"（被动方），B 说成\"影响他人的冲动\"（主动方）——方向恰好相反，这正是研究者要否定的 influentials 那一面。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"末段 not A but B 中的 B 就是 easily influenced people 的属性，C 把这个属性抽象为 readiness to be influenced——既不偏，也不强加，是末段结论句的最贴切转述。","pairs":[{"orig":"a critical mass of easily influenced people","opt":"The readiness to be influenced"},{"orig":"the principal requirement","opt":"the essential element"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"D 项 The inclination to rely on others。原文只说\"易被影响\"，不等于\"依赖他人\"——被影响是接受信息/态度，依赖他人则涉及生活/情感/决策的更广维度，D 比原文走得过远。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-4","kind":"reading","title":"Text 4","textNo":4,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 4","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-1","text":"Bankers have been blaming themselves for their troubles in public. Behind the scenes, they have been taking aim at someone else: the accounting standard-setters. Their rules, moan the banks, have forced them to report enormous losses, and it's just not fair. These rules say they must value some assets at the price a third party would pay, not the price managers and regulators would like them to fetch."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-2","text":"Unfortunately, banks' lobbying now seems to be working. The details may be unknowable, but the independence of standard-setters, essential to the proper functioning of capital markets, is being compromised. And, unless banks carry toxic assets at prices that attract buyers, reviving the banking system will be difficult."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-3","text":"After a bruising encounter with Congress, America's Financial Accounting Standards Board (FASB) rushed through rule changes. These gave banks more freedom to use models to value illiquid assets and more flexibility in recognizing losses on long-term assets in their income statements. Bob Herz, the FASB's chairman, cried out against those who \"question our motives.\" Yet bank shares rose and the changes enhance what one lobbying group politely calls \"the use of judgment by management.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-4","text":"European ministers instantly demanded that the International Accounting Standards Board (IASB) do likewise. The IASB says it does not want to act without overall planning, but the pressure to fold when it completes its reconstruction of rules later this year is strong. Charlie McCreevy, a European commissioner, warned the IASB that it did \"not live in a political vacuum\" but \"in the real world\" and that Europe could yet develop different rules."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-5","text":"It was banks that were on the wrong planet, with accounts that vastly overvalued assets. Today they argue that market prices overstate losses, because they largely reflect the temporary illiquidity of markets, not the likely extent of bad debts. The truth will not be known for years. But banks' shares trade below their book value, suggesting that investors are skeptical. And dead markets partly reflect the paralysis of banks which will not sell assets for fear of booking losses, yet are reluctant to buy all those supposed bargains."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-6","text":"To get the system working again, losses must be recognized and dealt with. America's new plan to buy up toxic assets will not work unless banks mark assets to levels which buyers find attractive. Successful markets require independent and even combative standard-setters. The FASB and IASB have been exactly that, cleaning up rules on stock options and pensions, for example, against hostility from special interests. But by giving in to critics now they are inviting pressure to make more concessions."}]},"questions":[{"n":36,"stem":"Bankers complained that they were forced to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"follow unfavorable asset evaluation rules."},{"key":"B","text":"collect payments from third parties."},{"key":"C","text":"cooperate with the price managers."},{"key":"D","text":"reevaluate some of their assets."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"银行家抱怨他们被迫____","choicesZh":{"A":"遵循不利的资产评估规则。","B":"向第三方收取款项。","C":"与价格管理者合作。","D":"重新评估他们的部分资产。"},"analysis":{"type":"Bankers complained that they were forced to____ 把答案锁定在一件具体行为上，不涉及推断或主旨。","parse":"Bankers complained that they were forced to____ 是“主句 + that 宾语从句”，从句里用“were forced to + do”被动结构，空格填动词原形短语；整句无陷阱，关键是 forced to 暗示“非自愿”。","locateEn":"Their rules, moan the banks, have forced them to report enormous losses, and it's just not fair. These rules say they must value some assets at the price a third party would pay, not the price managers and regulators would like them to fetch.","locateZh":"银行抱怨说，他们（指准则制定者）的规则迫使银行报告巨额亏损，这很不公平。这些规则要求银行必须按第三方愿意支付的价格给某些资产估值，而不是管理层和监管者期望的价格。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判“被迫执行不利于自己的估值规则”=follow unfavorable asset evaluation rules，follow=must do、unfavorable=not fair、asset evaluation rules=value assets 的规则，三处皆同义对齐，故选 A。","pairs":[{"orig":"These rules say they must value some assets at the price a third party would pay","opt":"follow unfavorable asset evaluation rules"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"collect payments from third parties 把 the price a third party would pay 里仅作“估值参照”的 third party 偷换成了“第三方付款方”，原文从未说银行真的向第三方收钱。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"cooperate with the price managers 凭空造出一个职业身份 the price managers，原文 the price managers and regulators would like them to fetch 里的 managers 指银行自己的管理层、不是“定价经理”，更没有合作关系。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"reevaluate some of their assets 与 value some assets at the price a third party would pay 看似都涉及“给资产估值”，但题干问的是“被迫做了什么遭抱怨之事”，答案应是“按某规则估值”，不是“重新估值”这一中性动作。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":37,"stem":"According to the author, the rule changes of the FASB may result in____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the diminishing role of management."},{"key":"B","text":"the revival of the banking system."},{"key":"C","text":"the banks' long-term asset losses."},{"key":"D","text":"the weakening of its independence."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"推断题","stemZh":"根据作者的观点,FASB的规则变更可能导致____","choicesZh":{"A":"管理层作用的削弱。","B":"银行系统的复苏。","C":"银行的长期资产损失。","D":"其独立性的削弱。"},"analysis":{"type":"may result in 表明答案是作者对 FASB 改动后果的判断，文中可能不会原句给出结论，需要根据立场句推断。","parse":"the rule changes of the FASB may result in____ 主干 the rule changes may result in X，of the FASB 是后置定语限定 changes 归属；空格填名词性短语作 result in 的宾语。","locateEn":"These gave banks more freedom to use models to value illiquid assets and more flexibility in recognizing losses on long-term assets in their income statements. Bob Herz, the FASB's chairman, cried out against those who \"question our motives.\" Yet bank shares rose and the changes enhance what one lobbying group politely calls \"the use of judgment by management.\"","locateZh":"这些（规则改动）给了银行更多用模型给非流动资产估值的自由，以及在损益表中确认长期资产损失的更多灵活度。FASB 主席 Bob Herz 怒斥那些“质疑我们动机”的人。然而银行股价应声上涨，新规增强了某游说团体委婉所称的“管理层的判断权”。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文 enhance what one lobbying group politely calls \"the use of judgment by management\" 明确说管理层判断权被“增强”，the diminishing role of management 恰好与原文相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"第 2 段 unless banks carry toxic assets at prices that attract buyers, reviving the banking system will be difficult 表明在作者眼中，目前的让步只会让复苏更难，the revival of the banking system 与作者判断相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"more flexibility in recognizing losses on long-term assets in their income statements 谈的是损失“在报表上如何确认”，是会计处理问题；the banks' long-term asset losses 把规则改动错误地等同为“引发”了银行的长期资产损失。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判“准则制定者独立性被削弱”=the weakening of its independence，its 回指 the FASB；其它三项均与原文事实或作者立场相违。","pairs":[{"orig":"the independence of standard-setters, essential to the proper functioning of capital markets, is being compromised","opt":"the weakening of its independence"},{"orig":"the use of judgment by management","opt":"the weakening of its independence"}]}}}}},{"n":38,"stem":"According to Paragraph 4, McCreevy objects to the IASB's attempt to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"keep away from political influences."},{"key":"B","text":"evade the pressure from their peers."},{"key":"C","text":"act on their own in rule-setting."},{"key":"D","text":"take gradual measures in reform."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据第4段,McCreevy反对IASB试图____","choicesZh":{"A":"远离政治影响。","B":"逃避来自同行的压力。","C":"在规则制定中独立行事。","D":"在改革中采取渐进措施。"},"analysis":{"type":"McCreevy objects to the IASB's attempt to____ 锁定到 McCreevy 反对的具体行为，是事实细节，限定 According to Paragraph 4。","parse":"McCreevy objects to the IASB's attempt to____ 中 attempt 后接不定式 to do 表“试图做某事”；空格填动词原形短语，注意 objects to 后的对象是“IASB 的尝试”，反对的是该尝试本身。","locateEn":"The IASB says it does not want to act without overall planning, but the pressure to fold when it completes its reconstruction of rules later this year is strong. Charlie McCreevy, a European commissioner, warned the IASB that it did \"not live in a political vacuum\" but \"in the real world\" and that Europe could yet develop different rules.","locateZh":"IASB 表示自己不想在缺乏总体规划的情况下行动，但等到今年晚些时候完成规则重构时，让其屈服的压力将很大。欧洲委员 Charlie McCreevy 警告 IASB，它不是“生活在政治真空中”，而是“生活在现实世界里”，且欧洲可能另起一套规则。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"keep away from political influences 是 not live in a political vacuum 的同义陈述，但这恰恰是 McCreevy 警告 IASB 不能做的事，不是 IASB 自己 attempt to 做的事；题干问的是 McCreevy 反对 IASB 想做什么。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"evade the pressure from their peers 中的 peers（同行）在原文找不到对应——压力来自欧洲部长与委员会，是政治/监管压力，不是“同行压力”。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判“反对 IASB 不顾政治现实、按自己节奏出规则”=act on their own in rule-setting：on their own 抓住“独自”这一核心，与 McCreevy “你不在真空里”的反讽完全对位。","pairs":[{"orig":"it does not want to act without overall planning","opt":"act on their own in rule-setting"},{"orig":"not live in a political vacuum","opt":"act on their own in rule-setting"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"take gradual measures in reform 谈“渐进改革”，原文 IASB 的表态是“要总体规划再动”而非“分步走”；gradual 在原文无对应。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":39,"stem":"The author thinks the banks were \"on the wrong planet\" in that they____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"misinterpreted market price indicators."},{"key":"B","text":"exaggerated the real value of their assets."},{"key":"C","text":"neglected the likely existence of bad debts."},{"key":"D","text":"denied booking losses in their sale of assets."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"推断题","stemZh":"作者认为银行\"身处错误的星球\"是因为它们____","choicesZh":{"A":"误读了市场价格指标。","B":"夸大了其资产的真实价值。","C":"忽视了坏账可能存在的事实。","D":"拒绝将资产出售中的损失入账。"},"analysis":{"type":"in that they____ 是因果连词 in that，要求从形象句推出作者所指的实际事实，答案是对原句的解释性同义替换。","parse":"The author thinks the banks were \"on the wrong planet\" in that they____ 主干 The author thinks (that) the banks were ...；in that 是因果连词，相当于 because；空格填动词短语解释“为何错”。","locateEn":"It was banks that were on the wrong planet, with accounts that vastly overvalued assets.","locateZh":"走错了星球的恰恰是银行——他们的账目上严重高估了资产。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"misinterpreted market price indicators 对应的是 they argue that market prices overstate losses——这是银行如今为自己辩解的话，而非作者用来论证 banks were on the wrong planet 的依据；题干问的是“为什么走错星球”，不是“银行如今怎么辩护”。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判“严重高估资产”=exaggerated the real value of their assets：exaggerated 对应 overvalued，real value of their assets 对应 accounts 高估的对象，正向一一对位。","pairs":[{"orig":"with accounts that vastly overvalued assets","opt":"exaggerated the real value of their assets"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 not the likely extent of bad debts 只说银行如今认为市价不能反映坏账规模，没有说银行“忽视坏账的存在”；neglected the likely existence of bad debts 把 the extent of（规模）偷换为 the existence of（存在与否），并把原本的 likely extent 抽象成完全忽视，过度推断。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"denied booking losses in their sale of assets 对应 banks which will not sell assets for fear of booking losses——这是文章对当前市场停滞的解释，发生在“走错星球”之后，与题干问的原因属于不同时间线。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":40,"stem":"The author's attitude towards standard-setters is one of____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"satisfaction."},{"key":"B","text":"skepticism."},{"key":"C","text":"objectiveness."},{"key":"D","text":"sympathy."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"态度题","stemZh":"作者对准则制定者的态度是____","choicesZh":{"A":"满意。","B":"怀疑。","C":"客观。","D":"同情。"},"analysis":{"type":"The author's attitude towards standard-setters is one of____ 直接问态度，是典型态度题，走特殊路径。","parse":"The author's attitude towards standard-setters is one of____ 主干为 attitude is one of X，one of 后接抽象名词；选项均为情感色彩名词，需根据全文情感极性匹配。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"satisfaction 要求作者对 standard-setters 当前状况感到满意，但 is being compromised 与 inviting pressure to make more concessions 都是负面处境描述，作者并不满意现状。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"skepticism 要求作者对 standard-setters 的能力或动机存疑，但 cleaning up rules on stock options and pensions, for example, against hostility from special interests 是明显的赞许；作者怀疑的是“让步会带来更多让步”的趋势，并非怀疑对象本身。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"objectiveness 要求作者保持不偏不倚，但全文从 essential to the proper functioning of capital markets 到 Successful markets require independent and even combative standard-setters 都明显站在 standard-setters 一边，并对其当下让步明确表达忧虑——这是带立场的同情，非客观中立。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判“认可对象、惋惜其处境”=sympathy：作者既高声肯定 independent and even combative standard-setters 的价值，又为其在压力下被迫让步而抱憾，整体语气与“同情”最贴。","pairs":[{"orig":"the independence of standard-setters, essential to the proper functioning of capital markets, is being compromised","opt":"sympathy"},{"orig":"by giving in to critics now they are inviting pressure to make more concessions","opt":"sympathy"}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-b","kind":"ordering","title":"Section II Part B 段落排序","directions":"Directions: For questions 41-45, choose the most suitable paragraphs from the list A-G and fill them into the numbered boxes to form a coherent text. Paragraph E has been correctly placed. There is one paragraph which does not fit in with the text. Mark your answers on ANSWER SHEET 1. (10 points)","points":10,"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-b-1","label":"A","text":"The first and most important is the consumer's growing preference for eating out: the consumption of food and drink in places other than homes has risen from about 32 percent of total consumption in 1995 to 35 percent in 2000 and is expected to approach 38 percent by 2005. This development is boosting wholesale demand from the food service segment by 4 to 5 percent a year across Europe, compared with growth in retail demand of 1 to 2 percent. Meanwhile, as the recession is looming large, people are getting anxious. They tend to keep a tighter hold on their purse and consider eating at home a realistic alternative."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-2","label":"B","text":"Retail sales of food and drink in Europe's largest markets are at a standstill, leaving European grocery retailers hungry for opportunities to grow. Most leading retailers have already tried e-commerce, with limited success, and expansion abroad. But almost all have ignored the big, profitable opportunity in their own backyard: the wholesale food and drink trade, which appears to be just the kind of market retailers need."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-3","label":"C","text":"Will such variations bring about a change in the overall structure of the food and drink market? Definitely not. The functioning of the market is based on flexible trends dominated by potential buyers. In other words, it is up to the buyer, rather than the seller, to decide what to buy. At any rate, this change will ultimately be acclaimed by an ever-growing number of both domestic and international consumers, regardless of how long the current consumer pattern will take hold."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-4","label":"D","text":"All in all, this clearly seems to be a market in which big retailers could profitably apply their gigantic scale, existing infrastructure, and proven skills in the management of product ranges, logistics, and marketing intelligence. Retailers that master the intricacies of wholesaling in Europe may well expect to rake in substantial profits thereby. At least, that is how it looks as a whole. Closer inspection reveals important differences among the biggest national markets, especially in their customer segments and wholesale structures, as well as the competitive dynamics of individual food and drink categories. Big retailers must understand these differences before they can identify the segments of European wholesaling in which their particular abilities might unseat smaller but entrenched competitors. New skills and unfamiliar business models are needed too."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-5","label":"E","text":"Despite variations in detail, wholesale markets in the countries that have been closely examined—France, Germany, Italy and Spain—are made out of the same building blocks. Demand comes mainly from two sources: independent mom-and-pop grocery stores which, unlike large retail chains, are too small to buy straight from producers, and food service operators that cater to consumers when they don't eat at home. Such food service operators range from snack machines to large institutional catering ventures, but most of these businesses are known in the trade as \"horeca\":hotels, restaurants, and cafés. Overall, Europe's wholesale market for food and drink is growing at the same sluggish pace as the retail market, but the figures, when added together, mask two opposing trends."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-6","label":"F","text":"For example, wholesale food and drink sales came to $268 billion in France, Germany, Italy, Spain, and the United Kingdom in 2000 – more than 40 percent of retail sales. Moreover, average overall margins are higher in wholesale than in retail; wholesale demand from the food service sector is growing quickly as more Europeans eat out more often; and changes in the competitive dynamics of this fragmented industry are at last making it feasible for wholesalers to consolidate."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-7","label":"G","text":"However, none of these requirements should deter large retailers (and even some large food producers and existing wholesalers) from trying their hand, for those that master the intricacies of wholesaling in Europe stand to reap considerable gains."}],"choices":[{"key":"A","text":"The first and most important is the consumer's growing preference for eating out: the consumption of food and drink in places other than homes has risen from about 32 percent of total consumption in 1995 to 35 percent in 2000 and is expected to approach 38 percent by 2005. This development is boosting wholesale demand from the food service segment by 4 to 5 percent a year across Europe, compared with growth in retail demand of 1 to 2 percent. Meanwhile, as the recession is looming large, people are getting anxious. They tend to keep a tighter hold on their purse and consider eating at home a realistic alternative."},{"key":"B","text":"Retail sales of food and drink in Europe's largest markets are at a standstill, leaving European grocery retailers hungry for opportunities to grow. Most leading retailers have already tried e-commerce, with limited success, and expansion abroad. But almost all have ignored the big, profitable opportunity in their own backyard: the wholesale food and drink trade, which appears to be just the kind of market retailers need."},{"key":"C","text":"Will such variations bring about a change in the overall structure of the food and drink market? Definitely not. The functioning of the market is based on flexible trends dominated by potential buyers. In other words, it is up to the buyer, rather than the seller, to decide what to buy. At any rate, this change will ultimately be acclaimed by an ever-growing number of both domestic and international consumers, regardless of how long the current consumer pattern will take hold."},{"key":"D","text":"All in all, this clearly seems to be a market in which big retailers could profitably apply their gigantic scale, existing infrastructure, and proven skills in the management of product ranges, logistics, and marketing intelligence. Retailers that master the intricacies of wholesaling in Europe may well expect to rake in substantial profits thereby. At least, that is how it looks as a whole. Closer inspection reveals important differences among the biggest national markets, especially in their customer segments and wholesale structures, as well as the competitive dynamics of individual food and drink categories. Big retailers must understand these differences before they can identify the segments of European wholesaling in which their particular abilities might unseat smaller but entrenched competitors. New skills and unfamiliar business models are needed too."},{"key":"E","text":"Despite variations in detail, wholesale markets in the countries that have been closely examined—France, Germany, Italy and Spain—are made out of the same building blocks. Demand comes mainly from two sources: independent mom-and-pop grocery stores which, unlike large retail chains, are too small to buy straight from producers, and food service operators that cater to consumers when they don't eat at home. Such food service operators range from snack machines to large institutional catering ventures, but most of these businesses are known in the trade as \"horeca\":hotels, restaurants, and cafés. Overall, Europe's wholesale market for food and drink is growing at the same sluggish pace as the retail market, but the figures, when added together, mask two opposing trends."},{"key":"F","text":"For example, wholesale food and drink sales came to $268 billion in France, Germany, Italy, Spain, and the United Kingdom in 2000 – more than 40 percent of retail sales. Moreover, average overall margins are higher in wholesale than in retail; wholesale demand from the food service sector is growing quickly as more Europeans eat out more often; and changes in the competitive dynamics of this fragmented industry are at last making it feasible for wholesalers to consolidate."},{"key":"G","text":"However, none of these requirements should deter large retailers (and even some large food producers and existing wholesalers) from trying their hand, for those that master the intricacies of wholesaling in Europe stand to reap considerable gains."}],"questions":[{"n":41,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"B"},{"n":42,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"F"},{"n":43,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"D"},{"n":44,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"G"},{"n":45,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"A"}],"order":["B","F","D","G","E","A"],"fixed":{"4":"E"},"chain":"41. → 42. → 43. → 44. → E → 45.","orderChain":"正确顺序 41 B → 42 F → 43 D → 44 G → 预给 E → 45 A","seams":["【引出后一段】 段 F 语义承接：B 作首段开篇立论，无显式段首回指，靠段尾论断把 F 的举证引出来 。41 是全文首位，前面没有锚邻段，B 段首 Retail sales of food and drink ... are at a standstill 不含任何回指词、第一次完整引入话题，独立开篇（弱锚：靠语义而非显式信号判其为首）。它向后的连贯靠段尾论断 just the kind of market retailers need 被 F 的数据承接，这条接缝在 42 题已坐实。","【承接前一段】 段 B 逻辑连接词：B 抛出「批发正是零售商需要的市场」论断，F 用 For example 拿数字佐证 。B 段尾 just the kind of market retailers need 是个待证实的论断，F 段首 For example 紧接着用 $268 billion 等数据为「这市场为何值得进」举证。论点（B）→ 例证（F）是最典型的顺承，故 F 接 B。","【承接前一段】 段 F 逻辑连接词：F 用 For example 列了一串卖点，D 用 All in all 把它们总括收口 。F 段是举证段，For example 领出 $268 billion、利润率更高、需求快增等并列卖点；D 段首 All in all, this clearly seems to be a market 的 All in all 正是对这串理由的总括。举证段（For example）后紧跟总括段（All in all），逻辑链顺承，故 D 接 F。","【引出后一段】 段 G 指代衔接：D 段尾抛出 New skills 等要求，正被 G 段首 these requirements 接住 。D 不仅承接 F，其段尾 New skills and unfamiliar business models are needed too. 又把门槛递给后文，由 G 的 these requirements 接走。两侧接缝都成立，D 落 43 位（F 与 G 之间）被双向钉死。","【承接前一段】 段 D 指代衔接：G 段首 these requirements 精确回指 D 段尾抛出的 New skills 等要求 。D 段尾 New skills and unfamiliar business models are needed too. 提出了一批「要求」，G 段首 none of these requirements should deter 用 these requirements 把它们指名接住并加以缓和（不该吓退零售商）。these+名词是最硬的回指，唯一着落点就是 D 段尾的 requirements，故 G 紧接 D。","【承接前一段】 段 E 指代衔接：A 段首 The first 正是 E 段尾承诺的 two opposing trends 之第一股 。E 在段尾明确预告 mask two opposing trends，A 段首 The first and most important is 的序数词 The first 唯一能消解的对象就是这「两股趋势」，于是 A 紧接 E。45 题位置在 given 段 E 的正下方，是全卷最稳的一处接缝。"]},{"id":"section2-part-c","kind":"translation","title":"Section II Part C 英译汉","directions":"Directions: Read the following text carefully and then translate the underlined segments into Chinese. Write your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. ( 10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-c-1","text":"One basic weakness in a conservation system based wholly on economic motives is that most members of the land community have no economic value. Yet these creatures are members of the biotic community and, if its stability depends on its integrity, they are entitled to continuance."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-2","text":"When one of these noneconomic categories is threatened and, if we happen to love it, we invent excuses to give it economic importance. At the beginning of the century songbirds were supposed to be disappearing. (46) Scientists jumped to the rescue with some distinctly shaky evidence to the effect that insects would eat us up if birds failed to control them. The evidence had to be economic in order to be valid."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-3","text":"It is painful to read these roundabout accounts today. We have no land ethic yet, (47) but we have at least drawn nearer the point of admitting that birds should continue as a matter of intrinsic right, regardless of the presence or absence of economic advantage to us."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-4","text":"A parallel situation exists in respect of predatory mammals and fish-eating birds. (48) Time was when biologists somewhat overworked the evidence that these creatures preserve the health of game by killing the physically weak, or that they prey only on \"worthless\" species. Here again, the evidence had to be economic in order to be valid. It is only in recent years that we hear the more honest argument that predators are members of the community, and that no special interest has the right to exterminate them for the sake of benefit, real or fancied, to itself."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-5","text":"Some species of trees have been \"read out of the party\" by economics-minded foresters because they grow too slowly, or have too low a sale value to pay as timber crops. (49) In Europe, where forestry is ecologically more advanced, the noncommercial tree species are recognized as members of the native forest community, to be preserved as such, within reason. Moreover, some have been found to have a valuable function in building up soil fertility. The interdependence of the forest and its constituent tree species, ground flora, and fauna is taken for granted."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-6","text":"To sum up: a system of conservation based solely on economic self-interest is hopelessly lopsided. (50) It tends to ignore, and thus eventually to eliminate, many elements in the land community that lack commercial value, but that are essential to its healthy functioning. It assumes, falsely, that the economic parts of the biotic clock will function without the uneconomic parts."}]},"sentences":[{"n":46,"en":"Scientists jumped to the rescue with some distinctly shaky evidence to the effect that insects would eat us up if birds failed to control them.","refZh":"科学家们赶忙出来救场，拿出了一些明显站不住脚的证据，大意是：如果鸟类不能控制昆虫，昆虫就会把我们吃光。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Scientists jumped to the rescue","lit":"科学家们跳出来救援","role":"（主干 主谓）","note":"难点： jump to the rescue 是固定搭配 Scientists jumped to the rescue 中 jump to the rescue 不是字面\"跳着去救\"，是\"赶忙出手相助、紧急驰援\"的习语；结合上文 songbirds were supposed to be disappearing，语境是科学家\"赶紧出来为鸣禽辩护\"。"},{"en":"with some distinctly shaky evidence","lit":"带着一些明显站不住脚的证据","role":"（方式状语（介词短语））","note":"难点： shaky 的态度色彩 some distinctly shaky evidence 里 shaky 字面\"摇晃的\"，此处熟词僻义为\"靠不住的、站不住脚的\"；distinctly 译\"明显地\"，整体带作者的负面评价，呼应全文 It is painful to read these roundabout accounts today. 的批判口吻，不能轻飘飘译成\"一些证据\"。"},{"en":"to the effect that insects would eat us up","lit":"其大意是：昆虫会把我们吃光","role":"（evidence 的同位语从句（由 to the effect that 引出））","note":"难点： to the effect that 是同位语连接词 to the effect that insects would eat us up 中 to the effect that 等于 \"meaning that / 大意是\"，引出 evidence 的具体内容；eat us up 不是字面\"把人吃掉\"，结合主语 insects 应理解为\"（虫害）把我们的庄稼/家底蚕食殆尽\"，可处理为\"会把我们吃光\"或\"会把我们的农作物吃光\"。"},{"en":"if birds failed to control them.","lit":"如果鸟类不能控制它们","role":"（条件状语从句）","note":"难点： them 的回指还原 if birds failed to control them 中 them 不能直接译\"它们\"，要回到前一块 insects would eat us up 还原为\"昆虫\"，否则汉语读者读不出指代；fail to do 译\"未能/不能\"比\"失败做\"更顺。"}]},{"n":47,"en":"but we have at least drawn nearer the point of admitting that birds should continue as a matter of intrinsic right, regardless of the presence or absence of economic advantage to us.","refZh":"但我们至少已经更接近于承认这一点：鸟类应当作为一种固有的权利继续存在下去，无论它们对我们是否具有经济价值。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"but we have at least drawn nearer the point of admitting","lit":"但我们至少已经更接近承认这一点","role":"（主干 主谓（含转折 but））","note":"难点： draw nearer the point of doing 的转译 we have at least drawn nearer the point of admitting 直译\"我们已被拉近到承认……的地步\"非常翻译腔；按汉语习惯转成\"我们至少已经更接近于承认……\"或\"我们至少已经开始愿意承认……\"；at least 体现作者的让步语气，要保留\"至少\"。"},{"en":"that birds should continue","lit":"鸟类应当继续存在","role":"（admitting 的宾语从句主干）","note":"难点： continue 的语境取义 birds should continue 中 continue 不要译\"继续\"那么空，结合上文 they are entitled to continuance 锚定为\"继续存在、存续下去\"，呼应全文\"存续权\"的主线。"},{"en":"as a matter of intrinsic right,","lit":"作为一种内在的权利","role":"（方式状语（介词短语））","note":"难点： as a matter of 的固定译法 as a matter of intrinsic right 中 as a matter of 是固定结构，意思\"作为……的事情、出于……\"；intrinsic right 译\"固有权利/内在权利/自身的权利\"均可，是本句核心采分概念，不能漏译\"intrinsic\"这个修饰。"},{"en":"regardless of the presence or absence of economic advantage to us.","lit":"无论对我们是否存在经济利益","role":"（让步状语（介词短语））","note":"难点： presence or absence 抽象名词具体化 regardless of the presence or absence of economic advantage to us 直译\"经济利益的存在或缺席\"很僵；把抽象名词 presence/absence 还原成动作\"有/没有\"，译\"不管对我们有没有经济利益\"或\"无论是否对我们具有经济价值\"。to us 表\"对我们而言\"，不能丢。"}]},{"n":48,"en":"Time was when biologists somewhat overworked the evidence that these creatures preserve the health of game by killing the physically weak, or that they prey only on \"worthless\" species.","refZh":"曾经有一段时间，生物学家有些过度地使用这样的证据：他们认为这些动物通过捕杀体弱的个体来维持猎物种群的健康，或者它们只捕食那些\"无价值的\"物种。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Time was when biologists somewhat overworked the evidence","lit":"曾经有一段时间，生物学家有些过度使用了这一证据","role":"（主干（Time was when… 倒装句型））","note":"难点： Time was when 是固定句型 Time was when biologists somewhat overworked the evidence 中 Time was when… 等于 \"There was a time when…\"，固定译\"曾经有一段时间……\"；overwork 不是\"过度工作\"，在此熟词僻义为\"过度使用、滥用\"；somewhat 是程度副词，译\"有些、多少有点\"，不可丢——它是作者的委婉批评。"},{"en":"that these creatures preserve the health of game by killing the physically weak,","lit":"这些动物通过杀掉体弱者来维持猎物种群的健康","role":"（evidence 的同位语从句①）","note":"难点： these creatures、game、physically weak 三个回指/僻义 these creatures 须回到段首 predatory mammals and fish-eating birds，译\"这些猎食性动物\"或\"这些捕食动物\"；game 在此熟词僻义为\"猎物（被捕食的野生动物）\"，绝不是\"游戏\"——是本句最阴的盲区；the physically weak 是\"the + 形容词\"表一类人/物，译\"体弱的（个体）\"。"},{"en":"or that they prey only on \"worthless\" species.","lit":"或者它们只捕食那些\"无价值的\"物种","role":"（evidence 的同位语从句②（与上句并列））","note":"难点： they 回指 + worthless 引号 they prey only on \"worthless\" species 中 they 同样回指 predatory mammals and fish-eating birds，可重复译为\"这些捕食动物\"或承前省作\"它们\"；\"worthless\" 加引号是作者反讽，译文要保留中文引号\"无价值的\"或\"所谓无价值的\"，体现态度；only 译\"只\"，限定范围不能丢。"}]},{"n":49,"en":"In Europe, where forestry is ecologically more advanced, the noncommercial tree species are recognized as members of the native forest community, to be preserved as such, within reason.","refZh":"在欧洲，那里的林业在生态层面更为先进，无商业价值的树种被视为本土森林共同体的成员，并以这样的身份在合理的范围内得到保护。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"In Europe, where forestry is ecologically more advanced,","lit":"在欧洲，那里的林业在生态学上更先进","role":"（地点状语 + 非限制性定语从句）","note":"难点： where 非限制性定语从句的处理 In Europe, where forestry is ecologically more advanced, 中 where 引导非限制性定语，按汉语习惯不能硬译成\"……的欧洲\"的前置长定语；拆成并列句\"在欧洲，那里的林业在生态学上更为先进\"或独立小句\"欧洲的林业在生态层面更先进，在那里……\"；ecologically 译\"在生态（学）上、从生态角度\"，是采分细节。"},{"en":"the noncommercial tree species are recognized as members of the native forest community,","lit":"无商业价值的树种被承认为本土森林共同体的成员","role":"（主干 主谓（被动））","note":"难点： 被动语态汉化 + 关键术语 the noncommercial tree species are recognized as members of the native forest community 是 are recognized as 被动结构；汉译可保留\"被承认为\"，或转主动\"（人们）将……视为/承认为\"；noncommercial=\"无商业价值的、非商业性的\"，呼应上文 economics-minded foresters 与 too low a sale value to pay as timber crops；the native forest community 与全文术语 the biotic community 保持一致，统一译\"本土森林共同体\"。"},{"en":"to be preserved as such,","lit":"并以这样的身份得到保护","role":"（目的/补充状语（不定式被动））","note":"难点： as such 的指代回还 to be preserved as such 中 as such 不是\"如此\"那么飘，它回指上一块的\"成员\"身份——意思是\"作为（共同体的）成员而得到保护\"，可译\"并以这样的身份/作为这样的成员而得到保护\"；to be preserved 是被动不定式，转主动可作\"加以保护\"。"},{"en":"within reason.","lit":"在合理的范围内","role":"（范围状语）","note":"难点： within reason 是固定搭配 within reason. 中 within reason 是固定短语\"在合理范围内、有分寸地\"，不是\"在理由之内\"；它收束整句、给\"保护\"加一个范围限定，避免被理解为\"无条件保护\"。"}]},{"n":50,"en":"It tends to ignore, and thus eventually to eliminate, many elements in the land community that lack commercial value, but that are essential to its healthy functioning.","refZh":"这种体系往往会忽视、并因此最终消灭土地共同体中的许多成分——这些成分虽然缺乏商业价值，但对土地共同体的健康运转却至关重要。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"It tends to ignore, and thus eventually to eliminate,","lit":"它往往忽视，并因而最终消灭","role":"（主干 主谓（含插入并列谓语））","note":"难点： It 回指 + 并列谓语夹注 It tends to ignore, and thus eventually to eliminate, many elements… 中 It 必须回到上句 a system of conservation based solely on economic self-interest，还原为\"这种（完全基于经济自利的）保护体系\"或承前简译\"它/这种体系\"；ignore 与 eliminate 是两个并列谓语，被两个逗号夹成\"插入\"形式，汉译要让它们都接到同一个宾语 many elements 上，常用\"往往忽视……乃至最终消灭\"或\"忽视并因而最终消灭\"。"},{"en":"many elements in the land community","lit":"土地共同体中的许多成分","role":"（宾语（含 in 介词短语作后置定语））","note":"难点： the land community 术语统一 many elements in the land community 中 the land community 是贯穿全文的核心术语，全篇统一译\"土地共同体\"；elements 在生态语境中译\"成分/要素/成员\"均可，本句指构成土地共同体的物种与组成部分。"},{"en":"that lack commercial value,","lit":"缺乏商业价值","role":"（限制性定语从句①（修饰 elements））","note":"难点： lack 译法 that lack commercial value 中 lack 是动词\"缺乏、没有\"；commercial value 译\"商业价值/经济价值\"，与全文 economic self-interest 主线呼应——这是被作者反对的衡量尺度。"},{"en":"but that are essential to its healthy functioning.","lit":"但对其健康运转必不可少","role":"（限制性定语从句②（与①并列，转折））","note":"难点： its 回指 + healthy functioning 抽象名词具体化 essential to its healthy functioning 中 its 须回到本句 the land community，译\"土地共同体的\"，绝不要留\"它的\"在汉语里飘；healthy functioning 是抽象名词短语，具体化为\"健康运转/正常运转\"，比直译\"健康的功能化\"自然得多。"}]}]},{"id":"section3-part-a","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part A 写作","directions":"51. Directions: You are supposed to write for the Postgraduates’ Association a notice to recruit volunteers for an international conference on globalization. The notice should include the basic qualifications for applicants and the other information which you think is relevant. You should write about 100 words on ANSWER SHEET 2. Do not sign your own name at the end of the notice. Use “Postgraduates’ Association” instead. (10 points)","prompt":"51. Directions: You are supposed to write for the Postgraduates’ Association a notice to recruit volunteers for an international conference on globalization. The notice should include the basic qualifications for applicants and the other information which you think is relevant. You should write about 100 words on ANSWER SHEET 2. Do not sign your own name at the end of the notice. Use “Postgraduates’ Association” instead. (10 points)","points":10,"image":null,"model":{"essay":"Notice June 20, 2026 The Postgraduates' Association is now recruiting volunteers for an upcoming international conference on globalization, which will bring together scholars from around the world. Applicants are expected to meet the following basic qualifications: fluent English for communication with foreign guests, a background related to economics or international relations, and enough free time during the conference week. The conference will be held from July 10 to 12 in the main hall. Those interested should send a brief application to pa@university.edu before June 30. For more information, please feel free to contact us at 010-12345678. Postgraduates' Association","translation":"通知 2026 年 6 月 20 日\n研究生会现为一场即将举办的全球化国际会议招募志愿者，本次会议将汇聚来自世界各地的学者。申请者须满足以下基本资格：英语流利、能与外宾沟通，具备经济学或国际关系相关的专业背景，并在会议期间有充足的空闲时间。\n会议将于 7 月 10 日至 12 日在主厅举行。有意者请于 6 月 30 日前将一份简短的申请发送至 pa@university.edu。如需了解更多信息，欢迎拨打 010-12345678 与我们联系。\n研究生会","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"标题日期就位","text":"【第 1 段】 标题日期就位 。Notice 单列居中、下写日期，落实了 outline 第一块‘标题与日期’，让人一眼看出是通知而非书信。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"目的加资格一段清","text":"【第 2 段】 目的加资格一段清 。开头 is now recruiting volunteers... 点明招募目的，随后 Applicants are expected to meet the following basic qualifications: 用三项并列把资格列全，落实the basic qualifications for applicants。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"其他信息全给到","text":"【第 3 段】 其他信息全给到 。The conference will be held...、Those interested should send... before June 30、please feel free to contact us at... 三句把时间地点、报名截止、联系方式补齐，覆盖the other information which you think is relevant。"},{"tag":"【第 4 段】","core":"机构落款守住","text":"【第 4 段】 机构落款守住 。结尾以 Postgraduates' Association 落款、未署真名，守住Use “Postgraduates’ Association” instead这条硬性要求。"}],"wordCount":98}},{"id":"section3-part-b","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part B 写作","directions":"52. Directions: Write an essay of 160-200 words based on the following drawing. In your essay, you should 1)describe the drawing briefly, 2)explain its intended meaning, and 3)give your comments. You should write neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2. (20 points)","prompt":"52. Directions: Write an essay of 160-200 words based on the following drawing. In your essay, you should 1)describe the drawing briefly, 2)explain its intended meaning, and 3)give your comments. You should write neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2. (20 points)","points":20,"image":{"src":"assets/writing/2010-english-one-section3-part-b.jpg","alt":"这是一幅黑白漫画，标题是“文化‘火锅’，既美味又营养”","width":"589","height":"604","local":"assets/writing/2010-english-one-section3-part-b.jpg"},"model":{"essay":"As is vividly depicted in the cartoon, a steaming hotpot is boiling on the table, in which various ingredients are cooking. Each ingredient is labeled with a cultural name, such as Confucianism, Taoism, Peking Opera and Kung Fu from China, along with Shakespeare, Einstein, Swan Lake and Enlightenment from the West. Above it reads a title: \"Cultural hotpot, both delicious and nutritious.\" Simple as it looks, the drawing conveys a thought-provoking message about cultural integration. The hotpot, which blends ingredients of different origins into one delicious dish, symbolizes an open and inclusive culture that absorbs the essence of both domestic and foreign traditions. Just as a hotpot tastes better when more ingredients are added, a culture grows richer when it embraces diverse elements rather than rejecting them. In an era of globalization, no culture can thrive in isolation. In my view, such cultural inclusiveness deserves our applause. We should keep an open mind, learning from other cultures while preserving our own roots. Only in this way can our culture stay nutritious and appealing.","translation":"正如漫画生动描绘的那样，桌上一口火锅正咕嘟冒着热气，锅里煮着各式各样的食材。每样食材都被标上了一个文化名称——来自中国的有儒、道、京剧、功夫，来自西方的有莎士比亚、爱因斯坦、天鹅湖、启蒙。火锅上方写着标题：“文化火锅，既美味又营养”。\n画面看似简单，却传递出一个发人深省的关于文化融合的信息。这口把不同来源的食材融成一道美味的火锅，象征着一种开放包容、能够吸纳中外传统精华的文化。正如火锅里食材越多越鲜美，一种文化在接纳多元元素而非排斥它们时，也会变得更加丰富。在全球化时代，没有哪种文化能够孤立地繁荣。\n在我看来，这种文化包容值得称赞。我们应保持开放的心态，既向其他文化学习，又守护自身的根脉。唯有如此，我们的文化才能始终富有营养、充满魅力。","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"套句总起加克制罗列","text":"【第 1 段】 套句总起加克制罗列 。本段用 \"As is vividly depicted in the cartoon\" 一句总起点出火锅主体，再以 \"Each ingredient is labeled with a cultural name, such as...\" 各举两三个中西例子，末句带出画中标题，落实描述段'总起＋两三处关键细节'的方法，完成 describe the drawing briefly 且篇幅克制。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"象征加类比把寓意说透","text":"【第 2 段】 象征加类比把寓意说透 。本段用 \"symbolizes an open and inclusive culture\" 把火锅意象绑定到文化融合，再以 \"Just as a hotpot tastes better when more ingredients are added\" 的类比坐实观点，末句 \"no culture can thrive in isolation\" 推到全球化背景，是全文得分重心，完成 explain its intended meaning。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"表态加对策再收束","text":"【第 3 段】 表态加对策再收束 。本段以 \"In my view, such cultural inclusiveness deserves our applause\" 亮明赞同态度，接 \"We should keep an open mind... while preserving our own roots\" 给出可落地对策，末句 \"Only in this way\" 倒装回扣中心，完成 give your comments。"}],"wordCount":173}}],"questionCount":45,"objectiveCount":45,"answerTable":{"ans-section1":"完形填空（四选一） Section I （1–20 题） 1 A affected · 2 B up · 3 C act · 4 B perplexing · 5 C accounts · 6 B matter · 7 D so long as · 8 A awareness · 9 C enough · 10 D by · 11 C subjected · 12 A Contrary to · 13 A evidence · 14 D misleading · 15 B For example · 16 A duly · 17 D continued · 18 C However · 19 B tended · 20 D hitting \n（逐题解析见 完形填空（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-1":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (1) （21–25 题） 21 B · 22 A · 23 D · 24 A · 25 B \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-2":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (2) （26–30 题） 26 C · 27 D · 28 C · 29 B · 30 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-3":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (3) （31–35 题） 31 B · 32 D · 33 A · 34 C · 35 C \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-4":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (4) （36–40 题） 36 A · 37 D · 38 C · 39 B · 40 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-b":"段落排序 Section II Part B 41=B → 42=F → 43=D → 44=G → 预给E → 45=A \n（逐题解析见 段落排序解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-c":"英译汉（划线句子翻译） Section II Part C \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 英译汉（划线句子翻译）解析页","ans-section3-part-a":"写作 Section III Part A \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页","ans-section3-part-b":"写作 Section III Part B \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页"},"coverage":{"objective":45,"explained":40,"missingSections":[]}};
